COLLDATA("qencen","en",[[1,"§Prologue\n﴿شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِي أُنزِلَ فِيهِ الْقُرْآنُ هُدًى لِّلنَّاسِ وَبَيِّنَاتٍ مِّنَ الْهُدَىٰ وَالْفُرْقَانِ ۚ فَمَن شَهِدَ مِنكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ ۖ وَمَن كَانَ مَرِيضًا أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِّنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ ۗ يُرِيدُ اللَّـهُ بِكُمُ الْيُسْرَ وَلَا يُرِيدُ بِكُمُ الْعُسْرَ وَلِتُكْمِلُوا الْعِدَّةَ وَلِتُكَبِّرُوا اللَّـهَ عَلَىٰ مَا هَدَاكُمْ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ ١٨٥﴾\nThe Holy Quran is the last book of revelation of Allah(swt) which He(swt) gave to His Last Messenger Muhammad(saws) and it contains the complete guidance for mankind. (See: Quran, Surah-2, Al-Baqara, Verse-185)\nThis Holy Quran was revealed in Arabic. More than six thousand scholars have written commentaries under various titles in order to bring to light the hidden gems in it. To date it has been translated into one hundred and twenty languages. A few scholars have made the ‘index’ of the words occurring in the Holy Quran. Among them the index created by Muhammad Fuwad Abdul-Baqi is the most popular. A French scholar Labome has divided the verses of the Holy Quran into eighteen parts and another French scholar Advar Monty, along with the French translation of the Holy Quran has also created an alphabetical index. All over the world, from east to west thousands of scholars are engaged in some or the other research pertaining to the Holy Quran. This is proof enough that the Holy Quran is a timeless miracle.\nMany translations and commentaries have been written in English. This is my humble effort in translating the book ‘Quran Majeed ki Encyclopedia’ written by Prof. Dr. Muhammad Zia-ur-Rehman Aazmi in Hindi. The book impressed me as being comprehensive which took into account the Holy Quran, the Sahih Hadith and historical evidence in explaining the various words occurring in the divine Holy Quran. I praise Almighty Allah(swt) who has given me the courage to take up this task and sincerely hope that it helps the reader in understanding this miraculous book from Allah(swt). I also hope that it helps in clearing up various misconceptions about the only religion in the sight of Allah(swt) namely Islam. If I am successful in my effort it is solely due to the infinite mercy of the Almighty(swt). Any shortcomings are due to my incompetence for which I beg the forgiveness of Ar-Rehman Ar-Raheem Allah(swt).\nTranslator"],[2,"§Good News\nDear readers! We are the progeny of the first human being Adam(as) – each and every one of us! So it is incumbent upon us that we have good and kind feelings towards each other. One of them is to wish for others what we wish for ourselves. I would never wish to lead a life without any governing rules, so that I be thrown into hell-fire after death. That is why the Almighty Creator of this entire Creation has sent a book which lays down the rules for leading a fulfilling life which will ultimately ensure everlasting success in paradise. This book is the Holy Quran. Allah(swt) has vouchsafed this divine book to His(swt) messenger Muhammad(saws) who was a living example of the Holy Quran. He(saws) has given glad tidings by every action of his that paradise can definitely be attained if we hold firmly to the word of Allah(swt) namely the Holy Quran.\nSo we should read the Holy Quran bearing in mind that this is a blessing for the entire mankind and that the Last Prophet(saws) has been sent as a mercy to all of us. Then you can understand the good news which I am giving. I have written this encyclopedia so that you may succeed in understanding the Holy Quran in its entirety.\nIt is you who will be able to judge whether I have succeeded in my goal or not."],[3,"§An important note\nI would like to inform my readers that originally the Holy Quran was revealed in Arabic. So, when we say ‘Allah(swt) says’ or ‘the Holy Quran says’, we mean this Arabic Quran. So, for easy understanding the translation of the verses of the Holy Quran is presented along with the original Arabic text.\nsaws: This is the short form of ‘Sallallahu Alaihi Wa Sallam’ which means ‘O Prophet! May the peace and blessings of Allah(swt) be upon you’.\nIt is incumbent upon all Muslims that when the name of the Holy Prophet(saws) is taken, we should pray for peace and blessings upon him. This is a command in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ وَمَلَائِكَتَهُ يُصَلُّونَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ ۚ يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا صَلُّوا عَلَيْهِ وَسَلِّمُوا تَسْلِيمًا ٥٦﴾\nIndeed, Allah confers blessing upon the Prophet, and His angels [ask Him to do so]. O you who have believed, ask [Allah to confer] blessing upon him and ask [Allah to grant him] peace.\n[Al-Ahzab: 56]\nas: This is the short form of ‘Alaihi Wa Sallam’ which has been used for the prophets other than Muhammad(saws) which translates as ‘may the peace of Allah(swt) be on them.’"],[4,"§A note for the readers\nThe topics are arranged according to the alphabetical order of the first letters of the words. Further ordering based on the remaining letters has not been done. So an index of the topics has been prepared so that the reader can choose any topic which he wishes to peruse."],[5,"§Definitions of various types of hadith\nHadith: The saying of the Holy Prophet(saws), his action or his silence on someone doing something are termed hadith. The effort put in by various scholars in collecting all the hadith of the Holy Prophet(saws) is unparalleled in any religion. In fact a new branch of knowledge has been formulated for this purpose which is called ‘Jarah-Taadeel’. And moreover new definitions had to be given to various types of hadith which was never done before. As quite a few definitions have been used in this book, it is necessary to explain their meaning.\nSahih: A Sahih hadith has to fulfill the following conditions:\nThe narrator should be ‘Aadil’; that is trustworthy with respect to his character.\nThe memory of the narrator should be strong and reliable. Or the hadith being narrated should have been written down.\nThe chain of narrators(Sanad) should be continuous(Muttasil); such that one narrator should have directly heard it from his teacher.\nNo ‘Shaaz’ thing should have been said with reference to the hadith.\nThere should be no form of ‘illat’ involved in the hadith.\nHasan: This is a hadith which fulfills all the conditions of a Sahih hadith. But the memory of the narrator is slightly weak. But not so weak that it can be qualified as ‘Zaeef’.\nZaeef: This is a hadith which does not fulfill a few of the conditions of a Sahih hadith.\nZaeef Jiddan: A narrator in the chain(Sanad) is very weak but not a liar.\nMauzzoo: This is not a hadith at all because it is something which some narrator has falsely attributed to the Holy Prophet(saws). It required lots of effort to search out the mauzoo hadith; so the scholars have written various books about them and wherever these occur, the scholars have made them clear so that nobody introduces their own opinions in Islam. That is why these mauzoo hadith have been mentioned in the books of hadith but their status has been made very clear.\nMutwatir: This is a type of hadith in which the narrators are so many that it is impossible for someone to lie about it. For a hadith to be Mutwatir, it has to fulfill the following two conditions:\nAt every step of the chain(Sanad), the narrators are so many that it becomes impossible for them to agree about some lie.\nMutwatir hadith should be perceived by one of the five sense organs.\nIllat: While researching the hadith, the flaws in the chain of narrators(Sanad) and Matan(the actual hadith) are termed illat. Illat is the reason why the hadith becomes Zaeef. Depending on the flaws, the illat in the hadith either increases or decreases. Sometimes illat is completely eliminated or sometimes it does not exist at all. For testing this, a profound knowledge of hadith is necessary. Famous scholars in this field are Imam Bukhari, Imam Darkhutni and Imam Baihaqi.\nMahfoos: This is a type of Sahih hadith. This is a hadith which is narrated by a more trustworthy(Aadil) narrator opposing a less trustworthy narrator. The narration of the more trustworthy narrator must be followed.\nShaaz: This is a hadith which a less trustworthy narrator narrates opposing a more trustworthy narrator(Aadil). It is not necessary to follow this hadith.\nMaaroof: This is a type of Sahih hadith whose narrator is Aadil(trustworthy) but some ‘Zaeef’ narrator narrates a hadith which goes against it. In that case the hadith of the Aadil narrator is termed ‘Maaroof’ and it is obligatory to follow it while the hadith of the ‘Zaeef’ narrator is termed ‘Munkar’ and it is forbidden to follow it.\nMunkar: This is a type of Zaeef hadith in which the narrator is not only Zaeef but also narrates this hadith opposing the hadith of an ‘Aadil’ narrator.\nMarfooah: This is a hadith which has been affiliated or connected to the Holy Prophet(saws). This can either be Sahih or Zaeef. If its chain(Sanad) or Matan(actual hadith) has no illat, then it is Sahih and if it has some illat, it will be Zaeef.\nMunqatah: This is a type of hadith in which there is at least one narrator in the Sanad(chain of narrators) who has not heard the hadith directly from his teacher. This is termed Munqatah, that is the chain of narrators(Sanad) has been cut. This is a Zaeef hadith because it does not fulfill the condition that the Sanad should be continuous.\nMaukhoof: This is actually not a hadith at all but can be found in the books of hadith. ‘Maukhoof’ means ‘to stop’. That is to stop connecting a hadith to the Holy Prophet(saws) and connect it to some sahaba or companion of the Holy Prophet(saws). So Maukhoof hadith comes under the category of Zaeef hadith but is actually not a hadith at all.\nMatan: Matan is the actual hadith which is expressed after the Sanad(the chain of narrators). A few books of hadith contain just the Matan; but these are not actual books of hadith but books written for the easy understanding of people. For example ‘Mishkaat’.\nSanad: Before expressing the actual hadith, the chain of narrators which is mentioned is called ‘Sanad’. This type of information is not found in any other religion.\nJamia: This is the book of hadith in which along with hadith, commentaries, Fiqh, Iman etc are also explained. For example: Jamia Sahih Bukhari, Jamia Sahih Muslim etc.\nSunan: This is the book of hadith written on the basis of religious commandments. For example Sunan Abu-Dawood, Sunan Nasai, Sunan Tirmizi, Sunan Ibn Maaja etc.\nMusnad: This is a book which has been written on the basis of the companions(sahaba). For example Musnad Ahmad.\nTaabai: A person who has met some sahaba(companion) of the Holy Prophet(saws) and obtained knowledge from him is called a tabai.\nMursal: This is a hadith which is narrated by a taabai as connected with the Holy Prophet(saws) when the taabai has never met the Holy Prophet(saws). For example when ‘Hasan Basri’ narrates: The Holy Prophet(saws) said “…………..”; then it is a mursal hadith. This is because ‘Hasan Basri’ is a taabai and there is no reference to any sahabi when the taabai must have heard it from some or the other sahabi.\nShaikh-ul-Islam: This is a title given to the scholars of hadith which is given to very few people. This is used for those scholars who have a very deep and profound knowledge of hadith, Fiqh and other branches of religious knowledge. For example ‘Ibn-Taimiya’.\nHaakim: This is a title of the scholars of hadith who have not only the knowledge of hadith but also a complete knowledge of Sanad and a widespread knowledge in other religious sciences also.\nHaafiz: The scholars of hadith who memorized the various hadith are called hafiz."],[6,"§Allah(swt)\n‘Allah’ is an Arabic word. It is derived from ‘Ilaah’ which means ‘worthy of worship’. Believing in Allah(swt) means that we worship Allah(swt) alone and ascribe no partners to Him. Verily there is only one Creator of this entire creation who is Allah(swt). That is why we do not worship anyone else other than the one Supreme Lord. Islam is based on the fundamental principle that we believe in the one God Allah(swt) and worship Him alone.\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nأَإِلَـٰهٌ مَّعَ اللَّـهِ ۚ تَعَالَى اللَّـهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ\nIs there a deity with Allah(swt)? High is Allah(swt) above whatever they associate with Him [An-Naml: 63]\nShirk is the greatest sin in the sight of Allah(swt) which He(swt) shall never forgive.\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ لَا يَغْفِرُ أَن يُشْرَكَ بِهِ وَيَغْفِرُ مَا دُونَ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ ۚ وَمَن يُشْرِكْ بِاللَّـهِ فَقَدِ افْتَرَىٰ إِثْمًا عَظِيمًا ٤٨﴾\nIndeed, Allah does not forgive association with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills. And he who associates others with Allah has certainly fabricated a tremendous sin. [An-Nisa: 48]\nThe Holy Quran is the last book of Allah(swt). In this revelation He(swt) has clearly explained His various signs and qualities(sifaat) and condemned shirk categorically. Every verse of the Holy Quran bears testimony to the fact that there is none worthy of worship other than Allah(swt). Today man has progressed so much in all spheres that he can easily understand the oneness of Allah(swt) and the fact that He(swt) alone is worthy of worship. But if he still persists in shirk he will have to bear the terrible everlasting punishment. So if any Muslim has failed to grasp this basic point he is still far removed from Islam."],[7,"§Aad\nAad was a very big tribe which inhabited the area between Oman and Hazar Maut. Some of the tribe lived in Ahqaf which is in the southern region of Saudi Arabia. The prophet Hud(as) was sent as a messenger to this tribe. But they rejected him; as a result of which they perished in a storm which lasted for seven nights and eight days.\n‘Aad’ was the name of the chieftain of the tribe. Not much is known about the history of this tribe. But we can deduce from the Holy Quran that it was a very prosperous tribe which was well known among the Arabs. They had even heard about the calamity which had befallen them. So, when this tribe was described again and again in the Holy Quran, nobody really needed more information about it. The grave of the prophet Hud(as) still exists in Hazar Maut; about 125 kilometers from the city of Mukalla. Every year a fair is also held here which proves that the people are well aware that this is the place where the tribe of Aad had lived. For more information see ‘Hud’ and ‘Al-Ahqaf’."],[8,"§Aakhirat(Hereafter)\nHuman life is divided into two parts. The first part is related to this world – it begins with his birth and ends with his death. It can be compared to the sowing stage of farming in which we can either sow good or bad seeds. We have been given certain rights in this part and our test lies in how we exercise these rights.\nThe second part is related to the time after death which is called Aakhirat(Hereafter). It begins with our worldly death and never ends. This can be compared to the harvesting and the consumption stages of farming. We shall reap the fruit of whatever seeds we have sown in the first part.\nFirst of all the Holy Quran commands us to believe in the Hereafter:\n﴿الم ١ ذَٰلِكَ الْكِتَابُ لَا رَيْبَ ۛ فِيهِ ۛ هُدًى لِّلْمُتَّقِينَ ٢ الَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَيُقِيمُونَ الصَّلَاةَ وَمِمَّا رَزَقْنَاهُمْ يُنفِقُونَ ٣ وَالَّذِينَ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكَ وَمَا أُنزِلَ مِن قَبْلِكَ وَبِالْآخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوقِنُونَ ٤﴾\nAlif, Lam, Meem. This is the Book about which there is no doubt, a guidance for those conscious of Allah - Who believe in the unseen, establish prayer, and spend out of what We have provided for them, And who believe in what has been revealed to you, [O Muhammad], and what was revealed before you, and of the Hereafter they are certain [in faith].\n[Al-Baqara: 1-4]\nBelief in the Hereafter is one of the main principles of Islam. Without this faith, no man can be a Muslim. It is imperative that man should worry more about the Hereafter than the life of this world because this worldly life will end in no time while the life of the Hereafter is for ever and ever.\n﴿يَا قَوْمِ إِنَّمَا هَـٰذِهِ الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا مَتَاعٌ وَإِنَّ الْآخِرَةَ هِيَ دَارُ الْقَرَارِ ٣٩﴾\nO my people, this worldly life is only [temporary] enjoyment, and indeed, the Hereafter - that is the home of [permanent] settlement.\n[Al-Momin: 39]\nSo, the Holy Quran urges us to worry more about the Hereafter:\n﴿قُلْ مَتَاعُ الدُّنْيَا قَلِيلٌ وَالْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّمَنِ اتَّقَىٰ وَلَا تُظْلَمُونَ فَتِيلًا ٧٧﴾\nSay, The enjoyment of this world is little, and the Hereafter is better for he who fears Allah. And injustice will not be done to you, [even] as much as a thread [inside a date seed].\"\n[An-Nisa: 77]\n﴿وَمَا الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا إِلَّا لَعِبٌ وَلَهْوٌ ۖ وَلَلدَّارُ الْآخِرَةُ خَيْرٌ لِّلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَ ۗ أَفَلَا تَعْقِلُونَ ٣٢﴾\nAnd the worldly life is not but amusement and diversion; but the home of the Hereafter is best for those who fear Allah, so will you not reason?\n[Al-An’am: 32]\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا مَا لَكُمْ إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمُ انفِرُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّـهِ اثَّاقَلْتُمْ إِلَى الْأَرْضِ ۚ أَرَضِيتُم بِالْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا مِنَ الْآخِرَةِ ۚ فَمَا مَتَاعُ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا فِي الْآخِرَةِ إِلَّا قَلِيلٌٌ\nO you who have believed, what is [the matter] with you that, when you are told to go forth in the cause of Allah, you adhere heavily to the earth? Are you satisfied with the life of this world rather than the Hereafter? But what is the enjoyment of worldly life compared to the Hereafter except a [very] little.\n[At-Tawba: 38]\n﴿اللَّـهُ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَن يَشَاءُ وَيَقْدِرُ ۚ وَفَرِحُوا بِالْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَمَا الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا فِي الْآخِرَةِ إِلَّا مَتَاعٌ ٢٦﴾\nAnd they rejoice in the worldly life, while the worldly life is not, compared to the Hereafter, except [brief] enjoyment.\n[Ar-Ra’d: 26]\n﴿وَمَا هَـٰذِهِ الْحَيَاةُ الدُّنْيَا إِلَّا لَهْوٌ وَلَعِبٌ ۚ وَإِنَّ الدَّارَ الْآخِرَةَ لَهِيَ الْحَيَوَانُ ۚ لَوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ ٦٤﴾\nAnd this worldly life is not but diversion and amusement. And indeed, the home of the Hereafter - that is the [eternal] life, if only they knew.\n[Al-Ankabut: 64]\nThat is why the Holy Quran chastises the people who think that this worldly life is everything and do not believe in the Hereafter.\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْآخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمْ أَعْمَالَهُمْ فَهُمْ يَعْمَهُونَ ٤﴾\nIndeed, for those who do not believe in the Hereafter, We have made pleasing to them their deeds, so they wander blindly.\n[An-Naml: 4]\n﴿وَأَمَّا الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا وَكَذَّبُوا بِآيَاتِنَا وَلِقَاءِ الْآخِرَةِ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ فِي الْعَذَابِ مُحْضَرُونَ ١٦﴾\nBut as for those who disbelieved and denied Our verses and the meeting of the Hereafter, those will be brought into the punishment [to remain].\n[Ar-Rum: 16]\nThat is the reason why we have been ordered to beg Allah(swt) more for success and peace in the Hereafter rather than worldly success.\n﴿فَإِذَا قَضَيْتُم مَّنَاسِكَكُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّـهَ كَذِكْرِكُمْ آبَاءَكُمْ أَوْ أَشَدَّ ذِكْرًا ۗ فَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا وَمَا لَهُ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنْ خَلَاقٍ ٢٠٠ وَمِنْهُم مَّن يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ ٢٠١﴾\nAnd among the people is he who says, \"Our Lord, give us in this world,\" and he will have in the Hereafter no share. But among them is he who says, \"Our Lord, give us in this world [that which is] good and in the Hereafter [that which is] good and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 200-201]\n﴿وَاكْتُبْ لَنَا فِي هَـٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ إِنَّا هُدْنَا إِلَيْكَ ۚ قَالَ عَذَابِي أُصِيبُ بِهِ مَنْ أَشَاءُ ۖ وَرَحْمَتِي وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ ۚ فَسَأَكْتُبُهَا لِلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَ وَيُؤْتُونَ الزَّكَاةَ وَالَّذِينَ هُم بِآيَاتِنَا يُؤْمِنُونَ ١٥٦﴾\nAnd decree for us in this world [that which is] good and [also] in the Hereafter; indeed, we have turned back to You.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 156]"],[9,"§Aasia\nThe wife of the Pharaoh(Firaun) was a very chaste and pious lady. She is not mentioned by name anywhere in the Holy Quran but according to Sahih Hadith her name was Aasia (Sahih Bukhari: 3411 and Sahih Muslim: 2431).\nIn the Holy Quran she has been depicted as an example of a very noble woman:\n﴿وَضَرَبَ اللَّـهُ مَثَلًا لِّلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا امْرَأَتَ فِرْعَوْنَ إِذْ قَالَتْ رَبِّ ابْنِ لِي عِندَكَ بَيْتًا فِي الْجَنَّةِ وَنَجِّنِي مِن فِرْعَوْنَ وَعَمَلِهِ وَنَجِّنِي مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ ١١﴾\nAnd Allah presents an example of those who believed: the wife of Pharaoh, when she said, \"My Lord, build for me near You a house in Paradise and save me from Pharaoh and his deeds and save me from the wrongdoing people.\"\n[At-Tahrim: 11]\nBy giving the example of the wife of the tyrant Pharaoh(Firaun), the Muslim ladies are being warned that without true faith and piety, their deeds are useless whatever be their station in this world.\nAasia is the one who coaxes Pharaoh(Firaun) to let her take care of Musa(as). Upon her insistence, Musa(as) was taken from the sea into the palace of Pharaoh(Firaun). The description occurs in Surah-28, Al-Qasas, Verse-9 of the Holy Quran. (For more information see ‘Musa’(as)).\n﴿وَقَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ فِرْعَوْنَ قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِّي وَلَكَ ۖ لَا تَقْتُلُوهُ عَسَىٰ أَن يَنفَعَنَا أَوْ نَتَّخِذَهُ وَلَدًا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ٩﴾\nBut it is given in Taurah Book Exodus, 2:4-10 that Musa(as) was picked up by Pharaoh(Firaun)’s daughter. It is possible that the person who actually picked up the baby from the sea was the daughter because even in the Holy Quran it is said that a member of the household of Pharaoh(Firaun) picked up the baby Musa(as) from the sea. Then when the baby was brought to the palace, Aasia requested Pharaoh(Firaun) to spare the baby so that they could adopt it. Please read the following verses from Surah Qasas carefully:\n﴿فَالْتَقَطَهُ آلُ فِرْعَوْنَ لِيَكُونَ لَهُمْ عَدُوًّا وَحَزَنًا ۗ إِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامَانَ وَجُنُودَهُمَا كَانُوا خَاطِئِينَ ٨ وَقَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ فِرْعَوْنَ قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِّي وَلَكَ ۖ لَا تَقْتُلُوهُ عَسَىٰ أَن يَنفَعَنَا أَوْ نَتَّخِذَهُ وَلَدًا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ٩ وَأَصْبَحَ فُؤَادُ أُمِّ مُوسَىٰ فَارِغًا ۖ إِن كَادَتْ لَتُبْدِي بِهِ لَوْلَا أَن رَّبَطْنَا عَلَىٰ قَلْبِهَا لِتَكُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ ١٠ وَقَالَتْ لِأُخْتِهِ قُصِّيهِ ۖ فَبَصُرَتْ بِهِ عَن جُنُبٍ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ١١ وَحَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَرَاضِعَ مِن قَبْلُ فَقَالَتْ هَلْ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ أَهْلِ بَيْتٍ يَكْفُلُونَهُ لَكُمْ وَهُمْ لَهُ نَاصِحُونَ ١٢ فَرَدَدْنَاهُ إِلَىٰ أُمِّهِ كَيْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ وَلِتَعْلَمَ أَنَّ وَعْدَ اللَّـهِ حَقٌّ وَلَـٰكِنَّ أَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ١٣﴾\nAnd the family of Pharaoh picked him up [out of the river] so that he would become to them an enemy and a [cause of] grief. Indeed, Pharaoh and Haman and their soldiers were deliberate sinners. And the wife of Pharaoh said, \"[He will be] a comfort of the eye for me and for you. Do not kill him; perhaps he may benefit us, or we may adopt him as a son.\" And they perceived not. And the heart of Moses' mother became empty [of all else]. She was about to disclose [the matter concerning] him had We not bound fast her heart that she would be of the believers. And she said to his sister, \"Follow him\"; so she watched him from a distance while they perceived not. And We had prevented from him [all] wet nurses before, so she said, \"Shall I direct you to a household that will be responsible for him for you while they are to him [for his upbringing] sincere?\" So We restored him to his mother that she might be content and not grieve and that she would know that the promise of Allah is true. But most of the people do not know.\n[Al-Qasas: 8-13]\nNow, the Taurah mentions that Musa(as) was adopted by the daughter of Pharaoh(Firaun) which does not seem plausible because it is generally the wife who does it and not the daughter. This is clear from the Holy Quran. In the Taurah, the events surrounding the birth of Musa(as) are given very briefly while they are given in great detail in the Holy Quran. So, it is possible that during the writing of the Taurah, small discrepancies may have crept in."],[10,"§Aayat\nAayat means sign, proof, evidence, lesson etc. The word aayat is used in the Holy Quran in three contexts:\nFirst meaning: In the Holy Quran aayat is used to mean a sentence and many such aayats combine to form a surah. For example, the lengthiest surah of the Holy Quran, Al-Baqara consists of 286 aayats while the shortest surah, Al-Asr consists of just three aayats.\nThe word aayat was first used in the Holy Quran in this sense because every sentence of the Holy Quran gives us numerous signs. For example in Surah Al-Baqara:\n﴿تِلْكَ آيَاتُ اللَّـهِ نَتْلُوهَا عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّ ۚ وَإِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ٢٥٢﴾\nThese are the verses of Allah which We recite to you, [O Muhammad], in truth. And indeed, you are from among the messengers.\n[Al-Baqara: 252]\nThese verses are in fact the revelations to the Holy Prophet(saws) from the Almighty(swt); a miracle which will be there till the Doomsday.\nSecond meaning: The word aayat also means a miracle. This is one of the miracles which had been given to the prophets. Like the miracle which was performed by Musa(as) by the grace of the Almighty(swt):\n﴿قَالَ أَلْقِهَا يَا مُوسَىٰ ١٩ فَأَلْقَاهَا فَإِذَا هِيَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعَىٰ ٢٠ قَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ ۖ سَنُعِيدُهَا سِيرَتَهَا الْأُولَىٰ ٢١ وَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ إِلَىٰ جَنَاحِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَاءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوءٍ آيَةً أُخْرَىٰ ٢٢﴾\n[Allah] said, \"Throw it down, O Moses.\" So he threw it down, and thereupon it was a snake, moving swiftly. [Allah] said, \"Seize it and fear not; We will return it to its former condition. And draw in your hand to your side; it will come out white without disease - another sign.\n[Ta-Ha: 19-22]\nThat is, the first aayat(miracle) was that the staff turned into a snake and the second aayat(miracle) was that his hand shone like the moon.\nThird meaning: In the Holy Quran, the word aayat is also used to mean ‘a sign’. At various places in the Holy Quran, Allah(swt) explains the various signs spread out in this world after which the disbelievers should not entertain the least doubt about the Sovereignty of Allah(swt).\n﴿وَجَعَلْنَا ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَأُمَّهُ آيَةً وَآوَيْنَاهُمَا إِلَىٰ رَبْوَةٍ ذَاتِ قَرَارٍ وَمَعِينٍ ٥٠﴾\nIn the same way Allah(swt) has made Isa(as), the son of Maryam and his mother the signs.\n[Al-Mu’minun: 50]\n﴿وَيُرِيكُمْ آيَاتِهِ فَأَيَّ آيَاتِ اللَّـهِ تُنكِرُونَ ٨١ أَفَلَمْ يَسِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ فَيَنظُرُوا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الَّذِينَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ ۚ كَانُوا أَكْثَرَ مِنْهُمْ وَأَشَدَّ قُوَّةً وَآثَارًا فِي الْأَرْضِ فَمَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُم مَّا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ ٨٢﴾\nAnd He shows you His signs. So which of the signs of Allah do you deny? Have they not traveled through the land and observed how was the end of those before them? They were more numerous than themselves and greater in strength and in impression on the land, but they were not availed by what they used to earn.\n[Momin: 81-82]\n﴿إِنَّ فِي اخْتِلَافِ اللَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمَا خَلَقَ اللَّـهُ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ لَآيَاتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَتَّقُونَ ٦﴾\nIndeed, in the alternation of the night and the day and [in] what Allah has created in the heavens and the earth are signs for a people who fear Allah.\n[Yunus: 6]\nIn this way Allah(swt) is cautioning the disbelievers and polytheists to change their ways or be the greatest losers in the Hereafter."],[11,"§Ababeel\nIt is generally assumed that ‘Ababeel’ is the name of a particular bird. But actually a flock of birds is termed ‘Ababeel’. The word is used to describe how flocks of birds descended on Abraha’s army and rained pebbles on them when he tried to attack the Holy Kaaba. The pebbles were such that they would go right through whoever was struck with them and reduce them to something resembling dry husk."],[12,"§Abdullah-bin-Ubai\nIn the Holy Quran, he is not mentioned by name but the person described in Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-11 is Abdullah-bin-Ubai.\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ جَاءُوا بِالْإِفْكِ عُصْبَةٌ مِّنكُمْ ۚ لَا تَحْسَبُوهُ شَرًّا لَّكُم ۖ بَلْ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۚ لِكُلِّ امْرِئٍ مِّنْهُم مَّا اكْتَسَبَ مِنَ الْإِثْمِ ۚ وَالَّذِي تَوَلَّىٰ كِبْرَهُ مِنْهُمْ لَهُ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ١١﴾\nIndeed, those who came with falsehood are a group among you. Do not think it bad for you; rather it is good for you. For every person among them is what [punishment] he has earned from the sin, and he who took upon himself the greater portion thereof - for him is a great punishment.\n[An-Noor: 11]\nIn the above verse, the person who carries the greater burden of sin upon his head is Abdullah-bin-Ubai who was the chief of the hypocrites. He was always the first to cause harm to the Holy Prophet(saws) or place hurdles in the propagation of Islam.\nDuring the war with the ‘Bani Mustaliq’ he got a chance to spread mischief and dissent and he tried to slander the name of Hazrat Aisha(ra) who was the wife of the Holy Prophet(saws). The description of the incident is as follows:\nWhenever the Holy Prophet(saws) embarked on a journey, he would decide which of his wives to take along by drawing lots. During the campaign of ‘Bani Mustaliq’ Hazrat Aisha’s(ra) name came up so she went along with the Holy Prophet(saws). This was after the verses making the hijab compulsory had been revealed. While returning from the battle they camped for the night at a place not far from Madina. Before dawn when they started making preparations for departure, Hazrat Aisha(sa) went out to relieve herself. On coming back, she noticed that her necklace was missing. Retracing her steps and after a long search, she found it. In those days a lady would sit inside a hawdaj(small tent placed on top of a camel) so that others would not see her. Then four men would lift it and place it on the camel’s back. Due to a long illness, Aisha(ra) had lost a lot of weight. So, the men thought that she was already in the hawdaj and placed it empty on the camel’s back. So, by the time she reached the campsite they had already packed up and left. She sat down and waited until someone returned to the campsite. After some time she fell asleep. Around dawn, Sufwan-bin-Mu’attal passed that way. He recognized her because he had seen her before the revelation of the verses concerning hijab. She woke up and immediately covered her face. He sat the camel near her and stood aside to one side. Aisha(ra) climbed onto it and he led the camel. About noon they caught up with the others. Reading the wrong meaning into this incident, some people slandered Hazrat Aisha(ra), the main person being Abdullah-bin-Ubai. But Aisha(ra) was unaware of what was being said about her.\nAfter reaching Madina she fell ill and was unwell for about a month. Meanwhile people continued to gossip and the Holy Prophet(saws) also came to hear of it. He(saws) became a little cold with her and Aisha(ra) kept wondering as to why her husband was not as affectionate to her as he was before her illness. She sought his permission and went away to her mother’s place for some time.\nOne day Aisha(ra) was walking with the mother of Mistah-bin-Usama. Mistah’s mother stubbed her toe and cursed “May you be destroyed Mistah”. When Aisha(ra) chided her for cursing someone who had fought in the battle of Badr, she answered, “Have you not heard what he is saying about you?” and then related the entire episode to her. Hazrat Aisha(ra) was extremely hurt and cried the whole night.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) summoned Hazrat Ali(ra) and Usama-bin-Zaid and sought their opinion about the whole issue. Usama-bin-Zaid answered, “O Prophet of Allah(swt) we have found nothing but piety in your wife.” Ali(ra) replied, “O Prophet of Allah(swt)! Allah(swt) has placed no constraint upon you. There are many other ladies. You can summon your slave-girl and question her. She will tell you all the facts.” When the slave-girl was questioned, she replied, “By the One Who Has sent you with the truth, I have never seen anything in her with which I may find fault. The only fault is that when I ask her to keep watch over the dough which I have kneaded, she falls asleep and the goat eats it away.” The same day the Holy Prophet(saws) gave a speech in which he expressed his sadness.\nThe rumours continued for about a month and they caused extreme sorrow to the Holy Prophet(saws) and Aisha’s(ra) parents while Aisha(ra) cried continuously. One day the Holy Prophet(saws) came to Aisha(ra), offered his salutations and sat down near her. He(saws) then said, “I have heard rumours about you. If they are false, I hope Allah(swt) will make your innocence clear. If you have committed a sin, repent before Allah(swt). When a slave accepts his guilt and seeks His forgiveness, Allah(swt) forgives him.” Hearing this Aisha(ra) wiped away her tears and turning to her father asked him to reply to the Holy Prophet(saws). He said that he did not know what to reply. When Aisha(ra) turned to her mother with the same request she got the same reply. Then Aisha(ra) said that they were simply believing the wild rumours. If she denied that she had committed a sin, they would not believe her while if she accepted that she had indeed committed the sin, they would believe her. So she said, “In the name of Allah(swt), I say what the father of Yusuf(as) had said that is ‘Fa-Sabrun-Jameel’(it is better to have courage and patience).” Saying this she lay down and turned away. She was thinking that Allah(swt) knows I am innocent and He(swt) will definitely make my innocence manifest. Aisha(ra) later relates that she never imagined that Allah(swt) would reveal verses proving her innocence and which would be read in the Holy Quran till Doomsday. She thought that maybe the Holy Prophet(saws) would have a dream proving her chaste and guiltless.\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) was still seated there when the verses started being revealed. In that condition even in winter beads of perspiration would start dripping from his face. Everybody was silent and waited for the mystery to be unraveled. Aisha(ra) was unperturbed. When the condition in which the revelations took place passed, the Holy Prophet(saws) appeared extremely pleased. He said, “O Aisha! Be happy. Allah(swt) has proved your innocence.” Then he recited the ten verses of Surah-24, An-Noor which had been revealed to him. Then Aisha’s(ra) mother said, “Get up and thank the Prophet of Allah(swt).” Aisha(ra) replied, “I shall neither thank him nor both of you but I shall thank Allah(swt) who has proved my innocence through His revelations.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 4750)\nOn the above occasion, the following verses were revealed:\n﴿إِنَّ الَّذِينَ جَاءُوا بِالْإِفْكِ عُصْبَةٌ مِّنكُمْ ۚ لَا تَحْسَبُوهُ شَرًّا لَّكُم ۖ بَلْ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ ۚ لِكُلِّ امْرِئٍ مِّنْهُم مَّا اكْتَسَبَ مِنَ الْإِثْمِ ۚ وَالَّذِي تَوَلَّىٰ كِبْرَهُ مِنْهُمْ لَهُ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ١١ لَّوْلَا إِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوهُ ظَنَّ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتُ بِأَنفُسِهِمْ خَيْرًا وَقَالُوا هَـٰذَا إِفْكٌ مُّبِينٌ ١٢ لَّوْلَا جَاءُوا عَلَيْهِ بِأَرْبَعَةِ شُهَدَاءَ ۚ فَإِذْ لَمْ يَأْتُوا بِالشُّهَدَاءِ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ عِندَ اللَّـهِ هُمُ الْكَاذِبُونَ ١٣ وَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللَّـهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِي مَا أَفَضْتُمْ فِيهِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ ١٤ إِذْ تَلَقَّوْنَهُ بِأَلْسِنَتِكُمْ وَتَقُولُونَ بِأَفْوَاهِكُم مَّا لَيْسَ لَكُم بِهِ عِلْمٌ وَتَحْسَبُونَهُ هَيِّنًا وَهُوَ عِندَ اللَّـهِ عَظِيمٌ ١٥ وَلَوْلَا إِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوهُ قُلْتُم مَّا يَكُونُ لَنَا أَن نَّتَكَلَّمَ بِهَـٰذَا سُبْحَانَكَ هَـٰذَا بُهْتَانٌ عَظِيمٌ ١٦ يَعِظُكُمُ اللَّـهُ أَن تَعُودُوا لِمِثْلِهِ أَبَدًا إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ١٧ وَيُبَيِّنُ اللَّـهُ لَكُمُ الْآيَاتِ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ١٨ إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يُحِبُّونَ أَن تَشِيعَ الْفَاحِشَةُ فِي الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ ۚ وَاللَّـهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنتُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ١٩ وَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللَّـهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ وَأَنَّ اللَّـهَ رَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٢٠ يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّبِعُوا خُطُوَاتِ الشَّيْطَانِ ۚ وَمَن يَتَّبِعْ خُطُوَاتِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَإِنَّهُ يَأْمُرُ بِالْفَحْشَاءِ وَالْمُنكَرِ ۚ وَلَوْلَا فَضْلُ اللَّـهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ مَا زَكَىٰ مِنكُم مِّنْ أَحَدٍ أَبَدًا وَلَـٰكِنَّ اللَّـهَ يُزَكِّي مَن يَشَاءُ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٢١﴾\nIndeed, those who came with falsehood are a group among you. Do not think it bad for you; rather it is good for you. For every person among them is what [punishment] he has earned from the sin, and he who took upon himself the greater portion thereof - for him is a great punishment. Why, when you heard it, did not the believing men and believing women think good of one another and say, \"This is an obvious falsehood\"? Why did they [who slandered] not produce for it four witnesses? And when they do not produce the witnesses, then it is they, in the sight of Allah, who are the liars. And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy in this world and the Hereafter, you would have been touched for that [lie] in which you were involved by a great punishment. When you received it with your tongues and said with your mouths that of which you had no knowledge and thought it was insignificant while it was, in the sight of Allah, tremendous. And why, when you heard it, did you not say, \"It is not for us to speak of this. Exalted are You, [O Allah]; this is a great slander\"? Allah warns you against returning to the likes of this [conduct], ever, if you should be believers. And Allah makes clear to you the verses, and Allah is Knowing and Wise. Indeed, those who like that immorality should be spread [or publicized] among those who have believed will have a painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter. And Allah knows and you do not know. And if it had not been for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy... and because Allah is Kind and Merciful. O you who have believed, do not follow the footsteps of Satan. And whoever follows the footsteps of Satan - indeed, he enjoins immorality and wrongdoing. And if not for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy, not one of you would have been pure, ever, but Allah purifies whom He wills, and Allah is Hearing and Knowing. [An-Noor: 11-21]\nAnd this is the chief of the hypocrites, Abdullah-bin-Ubai, who had said during the campaign of Bani-Mustaliq:\n﴿يَقُولُونَ لَئِن رَّجَعْنَا إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ الْأَعَزُّ مِنْهَا الْأَذَلَّ ۚ وَلِلَّـهِ الْعِزَّةُ وَلِرَسُولِهِ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَلَـٰكِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ ٨﴾\nThey say, \"If we return to Al-Madinah, the more honored [for power] will surely expel therefrom the more humble.\" And to Allah belongs [all] honor, and to His Messenger, and to the believers, but the hypocrites do not know.\n[Al-Munafiqun: 8]\nHis son, Abdullah-bin-Abdullah-bin-Ubai had embraced Islam before this incident. He sought the permission of the Holy Prophet(saws) to kill his father. But the Holy Prophet(saws) refused. A few days later when he died, his son asked the Holy Prophet(saws) for his garment to cover his father’s body. The Holy Prophet(saws) relented. Then he requested him to offer his father’s funeral prayer. The Holy Prophet(saws) did so because he was sent as a mercy to the whole mankind. This act of his always saddened the Holy Prophet(saws) and also all the Muslims. With regard to this incident, the following verse of the Holy Quran was revealed:\n﴿وَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلَىٰ أَحَدٍ مِّنْهُم مَّاتَ أَبَدًا وَلَا تَقُمْ عَلَىٰ قَبْرِهِ ۖ إِنَّهُمْ كَفَرُوا بِاللَّـهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَمَاتُوا وَهُمْ فَاسِقُونَ ٨٤﴾\nAnd do not pray [the funeral prayer, O Muhammad], over any of them who has died - ever - or stand at his grave. Indeed, they disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger and died while they were defiantly disobedient.\n[At-Tawba: 84]"],[13,"§Ablution(Wudu)\nAblution or Wudu is compulsory for performing salah. Salah is invalid without this as mentioned both in the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith.\nMethod of performing Wudu:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِذَا قُمْتُمْ إِلَى الصَّلَاةِ فَاغْسِلُوا وُجُوهَكُمْ وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ إِلَى الْمَرَافِقِ وَامْسَحُوا بِرُءُوسِكُمْ وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ إِلَى الْكَعْبَيْنِ ۚ وَإِن كُنتُمْ جُنُبًا فَاطَّهَّرُوا ۚ وَإِن كُنتُم مَّرْضَىٰ أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍ أَوْ جَاءَ أَحَدٌ مِّنكُم مِّنَ الْغَائِطِ أَوْ لَامَسْتُمُ النِّسَاءَ فَلَمْ تَجِدُوا مَاءً فَتَيَمَّمُوا صَعِيدًا طَيِّبًا فَامْسَحُوا بِوُجُوهِكُمْ وَأَيْدِيكُم مِّنْهُ ۚ مَا يُرِيدُ اللَّـهُ لِيَجْعَلَ عَلَيْكُم مِّنْ حَرَجٍ وَلَـٰكِن يُرِيدُ لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ وَلِيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ ٦﴾\nO you who have believed, when you rise to [perform] prayer, wash your faces and your forearms to the elbows and wipe over your heads and wash your feet to the ankles.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 6]\nIt is mentioned in the Sahih Hadith that before dipping the hands in the water, they should be washed thrice, then the mouth should be gargled with water thrice, then the nose should be cleansed by passing water through it thrice, then the face should be washed thrice, then the hands should be washed thrice till the elbows, then the head should be wiped once with wet hands(masah), then the feet should be washed till the ankles thrice. Then the wudu is complete.\nThis is called wudu without which namaz is not accepted. But after performing wudu, if the person is still in a state of wudu, the next namaz can be offered without repeating the wudu.\nThe things which nullify an ablution:\nIntercourse.\nAttending the call of nature.\nSleeping.\nPassing wind.\nMenses and Istihaajaa.\nBecoming unconscious.\nBecoming intoxicated.\nEating the meat of camel.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that vomiting and touching private parts also nullify the wudu. But the hadith regarding this is not very reliable."],[14,"§Abu-Bakr-Siddique\nAbu-Bakr-Siddique was among the most esteemed of the companions of the Holy Prophet(saws). He is not mentioned directly in the Holy Quran but is described indirectly in the following verse:\n﴿إِلَّا تَنصُرُوهُ فَقَدْ نَصَرَهُ اللَّـهُ إِذْ أَخْرَجَهُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ إِذْ هُمَا فِي الْغَارِ إِذْ يَقُولُ لِصَاحِبِهِ لَا تَحْزَنْ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ مَعَنَا ۖ فَأَنزَلَ اللَّـهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَيْهِ وَأَيَّدَهُ بِجُنُودٍ لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا وَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا السُّفْلَىٰ ۗ وَكَلِمَةُ اللَّـهِ هِيَ الْعُلْيَا ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ ٤٠﴾\nIf you do not aid the Prophet - Allah has already aided him when those who disbelieved had driven him out [of Makkah] as one of two, when they were in the cave and he said to his companion, \"Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us.\" And Allah sent down his tranquillity upon him and supported him with angels you did not see and made the word of those who disbelieved the lowest, while the word of Allah - that is the highest. And Allah is Exalted in Might and Wise.\n[At-Tawba: 40]\nThe reference is to Abu-Bakr-Siddique in ‘one of two’ in the above verse. All the commentators are unanimous in their opinion that the second person or ‘one of two’ is none other than Abu-Bakr. The word used in the Holy Quran is ‘Saniya Sanain’, so he is also called as ‘Saniya Sanain’. When the Holy Prophet(saws) migrated from Mecca, Abu-Bakr was with the Holy Prophet(saws) and as the disbelievers were following them, they hid in a cave named ‘Saur’. The enemies reached the mouth of the cave in search of them. Abu-Bakr was scared that they would find them. But the Holy Prophet(saws) was calm and composed and soothed Abu-Bakr because it was only by the command of Allah(swt) that they had migrated. Allah(swt) made peace to descend upon them.\nThe 40th verse of the Surah At-Tawba refers to this incident and in reality Abu-Bakr became ‘one of two’ because during his lifetime itself, the Holy Prophet(saws) indicated that Abu-Bakr would be the Caliph after him and the Muslims took baith(pledge) on his hand after the demise of the Holy Prophet(saws). He became the first Caliph of the Muslims. He was two years younger to the Holy Prophet(saws) and he passed away exactly two years after the Holy Prophet(saws). So, he was the same age as the Holy Prophet(saws) at the time of his death. He was buried near the Holy Prophet(saws)."],[15,"§Abu-Lahab\nThe Holy Quran has a surah by the name ‘Lahab’. It is even called ‘Tabbat-Yada’.\n﴿تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِي لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ ١ مَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُ مَالُهُ وَمَا كَسَبَ ٢ سَيَصْلَىٰ نَارًا ذَاتَ لَهَبٍ ٣ وَامْرَأَتُهُ حَمَّالَةَ الْحَطَبِ ٤ فِي جِيدِهَا حَبْلٌ مِّن مَّسَدٍ ٥﴾\nMay the hands of Abu Lahab be ruined, and ruined is he. His wealth will not avail him or that which he gained. He will [enter to] burn in a Fire of [blazing] flame. And his wife [as well] - the carrier of firewood. Around her neck is a rope of [twisted] fiber.\n[Al-Lahab: 1-5]\nUzza-bin-Abdul Mutallib was the name of Abu-Lahab. He was the paternal uncle of the Holy Prophet(saws). The houses of Abu-Lahab and Prophet Muhammad(saws) were joined together. It was his duty to take care of his orphaned nephew, Muhammad(saws), but instead he became his sworn enemy and was foremost among the disbelievers of the religion advocated by the Holy Prophet(saws). He persecuted the Messenger(saws) in many ways. Wherever the Holy Prophet(saws) went to propagate Islam, he would follow him there and tell the people “He is a liar. Do not believe him”. When Allah(swt) instructed Muhammad(saws) to first warn his close relatives about the punishment of Allah(swt), according to the Arab custom, the Prophet(saws) climbed the mountain ‘Safa’ and called out to the people “O Sahaba, (meaning people), fear the enemy”. Hearing this when the people assembled, the Prophet(saws) shouted out to the people of Quraish “O my people! If I tell you that an enemy is lurking behind this mountain who is going to attack you, will you believe me?” The people answered, “We surely will because you have never uttered any lie.” Then the Prophet(saws) said “I warn you of a terrible punishment from Allah(swt) if you do not believe in my message.”\nHearing this the people remained silent, but Abu-Lahab became furious and said “May you be destroyed. Is this why you have assembled us?” (Sahih Bukhari, 4971 and Sahih Muslim, 208)\nAccording to a Sahih Hadith he even picked up a stone for hitting the Holy Prophet(saws).\nAccording to another Hadith, Abu-Lahab once asked the Holy Prophet(saws), “If I accept your religion, what will I get?” The Holy Prophet(saws) answered, “The same as what the other believers get.” He then asked, “Will I not get something better?” The Holy Prophet asked, “What else do you want?” He became furious at this and said “May your religion be destroyed in which I and the other people are equal.”\nUpon this Allah(swt) revealed the Surah ‘Lahab’. Abu Lahab had turned such a bitter enemy of the Holy Prophet(saws) that he asked both his sons, Utaiba and Utba who happened to be the sons-in-law of the Holy Prophet(saws) to divorce Muhammad(saws)’s daughters. Both of them divorced the daughters of the Holy Prophet(saws) and Utaiba became the Holy Prophet(saws)’s bitter enemy. One day, he tried to spit upon the Holy Prophet(saws), but Allah(swt) saved him(saws). The Holy Prophet(saws) cursed him saying that may Allah(swt) cause an animal of prey to sit on your head. Allah(swt) fulfilled his curse and on a journey to Syria he was torn to pieces and eaten by a lion.\nWith regard to Abu-Lahab, Allah(swt) says that his wealth and all that he earned did not avail him, and the absolute truth prevailed. Seven to eight years after this verse was revealed, in the battle of Badr, the disbelievers of Mecca were defeated and after a few days Abu-Lahab fell ill. He died due to small-pox. For three to four days his body lay rotting. None of his children was ready to bury it. Then, some African slaves were paid some money to dump his body in a hole and it was covered up with mud and stones. His other sons Utba, Mut’ab and daughter Duri embraced Islam and after coming to Madina took the ‘Baith’ on the hand of the Holy Prophet(saws). For the explanation about the wife of Abu-Lahab see ‘Hammalatal-Hatab.’"],[16,"§Accusation\nSee ‘Khazaf’."],[17,"§Adam(as)\nAdam is a Hebrew word which means ‘wheat complexioned’. Adam(as) is the father of mankind whom Allah(swt) created from dust and breathed His soul in him. He(swt) ordered the angels to prostrate in front of him. Everybody obeyed except the leader of the satans – the Iblees[Al-Hijr: 28-31] [Sad: 72-74]. When Allah(swt) asked him the reason, he replied:\n﴿قَالَ مَا مَنَعَكَ أَلَّا تَسْجُدَ إِذْ أَمَرْتُكَ ۖ قَالَ أَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْهُ خَلَقْتَنِي مِن نَّارٍ وَخَلَقْتَهُ مِن طِينٍ ١٢﴾\n[Allah] said, \"What prevented you from prostrating when I commanded you?\" [Satan] said, \"I am better than him. You created me from fire and created him from clay.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 12]\nAllah(swt) was displeased with this disobedience and He(swt) banished Iblees from heaven.\nWhen Allah(swt) decided to create and appoint Adam(as) as the vicegerent of the creatures of the earth, the angels were surprised and asked Allah(swt) as to why He(swt) was doing so when they were exalting Him with His praises night and day. Allah(swt) said:\n﴿قَالَ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ مَا لَا تَعْلَمُونَ ٣٠﴾\nAllah(swt) said, \"Indeed, I know that which you do not know.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 30]\n﴿وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الْأَسْمَاءَ كُلَّهَا ثُمَّ عَرَضَهُمْ عَلَى الْمَلَائِكَةِ فَقَالَ أَنبِئُونِي بِأَسْمَاءِ هَـٰؤُلَاءِ إِن كُنتُمْ صَادِقِينَ ٣١ قَالُوا سُبْحَانَكَ لَا عِلْمَ لَنَا إِلَّا مَا عَلَّمْتَنَا ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْعَلِيمُ الْحَكِيمُ ٣٢ قَالَ يَا آدَمُ أَنبِئْهُم بِأَسْمَائِهِمْ ۖ فَلَمَّا أَنبَأَهُم بِأَسْمَائِهِمْ قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ إِنِّي أَعْلَمُ غَيْبَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَأَعْلَمُ مَا تُبْدُونَ وَمَا كُنتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ ٣٣﴾\nAnd He(swt) taught Adam the names - all of them. Then He showed them to the angels and said, \"Inform Me of the names of these, if you are truthful.\" They said, \"Exalted are You; we have no knowledge except what You have taught us. Indeed, it is You who is the Knowing, the Wise.\" He said, \"O Adam, inform them of their names.\" And when he had informed them of their names, He said, \"Did I not tell you that I know the unseen [aspects] of the heavens and the earth? And I know what you reveal and what you have concealed.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 31-33]\nThen Allah(swt) created Eve from Adam(as):\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ اتَّقُوا رَبَّكُمُ الَّذِي خَلَقَكُم مِّن نَّفْسٍ وَاحِدَةٍ وَخَلَقَ مِنْهَا زَوْجَهَا وَبَثَّ مِنْهُمَا رِجَالًا كَثِيرًا وَنِسَاءً ۚ وَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ الَّذِي تَسَاءَلُونَ بِهِ وَالْأَرْحَامَ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ كَانَ عَلَيْكُمْ رَقِيبًا ١﴾\nO mankind, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate and dispersed from both of them many men and women.\n[An-Nisa: 1]\nIt says in the Taurah that Eve was created from the rib of Adam(as).\nIt is not surprising that Eve was created from the side rib of Adam(as) because when Allah(swt) can create Adam(as) from mud, it is not difficult for Him to create Eve from Adam(as)’s rib. Then Allah(swt) asked Adam(as) and Eve to stay in heaven and eat and drink whatever they pleased. But as a test for them, He asked them not to eat the fruit of a particular tree. But the Satan coaxed them to go near the tree and told them that their Lord(swt) had forbidden them the fruit of that tree lest they turn into angels. Or that they may stay in heaven forever. So, both of them ate the fruit of that tree. Allah(swt) ordered them to descend to the earth and stay there for a prescribed period.\nWhen Adam(as) realized that they had been led astray by the Satan, he repented and begged Allah(swt)’s forgiveness.\n﴿وَقُلْنَا يَا آدَمُ اسْكُنْ أَنتَ وَزَوْجُكَ الْجَنَّةَ وَكُلَا مِنْهَا رَغَدًا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمَا وَلَا تَقْرَبَا هَـٰذِهِ الشَّجَرَةَ فَتَكُونَا مِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ ٣٥ فَأَزَلَّهُمَا الشَّيْطَانُ عَنْهَا فَأَخْرَجَهُمَا مِمَّا كَانَا فِيهِ ۖ وَقُلْنَا اهْبِطُوا بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ ۖ وَلَكُمْ فِي الْأَرْضِ مُسْتَقَرٌّ وَمَتَاعٌ إِلَىٰ حِينٍ ٣٦﴾\nAnd We said, \"O Adam, dwell, you and your wife, in Paradise and eat therefrom in [ease and] abundance from wherever you will. But do not approach this tree, lest you be among the wrongdoers.\" But Satan caused them to slip out of it and removed them from that [condition] in which they had been. And We said, \"Go down, [all of you], as enemies to one another, and you will have upon the earth a place of settlement and provision for a time.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 35-36]\nIn this way both Adam(as) and Eve started living on the earth. They had two sons – (Cain)Qabil and Habil(Abel). Cain means a blacksmith and Habil means a son. Adam(as) married the twin sister of one brother with the other brother. Qabil killed his brother Habil. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَاتْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ نَبَأَ ابْنَيْ آدَمَ بِالْحَقِّ إِذْ قَرَّبَا قُرْبَانًا فَتُقُبِّلَ مِنْ أَحَدِهِمَا وَلَمْ يُتَقَبَّلْ مِنَ الْآخَرِ قَالَ لَأَقْتُلَنَّكَ ۖ قَالَ إِنَّمَا يَتَقَبَّلُ اللَّـهُ مِنَ الْمُتَّقِينَ ٢٧﴾\nAnd recite to them the story of Adam's two sons, in truth, when they both offered a sacrifice [to Allah], and it was accepted from one of them but was not accepted from the other. Said [the latter], \"I will surely kill you.\" Said [the former], \"Indeed, Allah only accepts from the righteous [who fear Him].\n[Al-Ma’ida: 27]\nAccording to the Taurah, Habil was a shepherd and so he offered a sacrifice of fat portions from some of the firstborn of his flock which was accepted by Allah(swt) while Qabil who tilled his land offered a gift of fruit which was not accepted from him. In anger, he killed his brother Habil. (Genesis 4:2-9) After that Qabil did not know what to do with the body of his brother. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿فَبَعَثَ اللَّـهُ غُرَابًا يَبْحَثُ فِي الْأَرْضِ لِيُرِيَهُ كَيْفَ يُوَارِي سَوْءَةَ أَخِيهِ ۚ قَالَ يَا وَيْلَتَىٰ أَعَجَزْتُ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِثْلَ هَـٰذَا الْغُرَابِ فَأُوَارِيَ سَوْءَةَ أَخِي ۖ فَأَصْبَحَ مِنَ النَّادِمِينَ ٣١﴾\nThen Allah sent a crow searching in the ground to show him how to hide the disgrace of his brother. He said, \"O woe to me! Have I failed to be like this crow and hide the body of my brother?\" And he became of the regretful.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 31]\nIn this way man learned how to bury the dead.\nAccording to Sahih Bukhari, Abdullah-bin-Masood narrated that the Holy Prophet(saws) said:\nWhenever a murder takes place, the first son of Adam(as) gets a part of the sin because he was the one who first started the system of killing.\n(Sahih Bukhari: Kitabul Anbiya 33-35)\nAfter the killing of Habil, Adam(as) and Eve had another son named Seth which means ‘in place of’ that is Seth was given in place of Habil who was killed by his brother Qabil. Then from these two namely Qabil and Seth, all the human beings were born. (Genesis 4:25, 5:3)\nAccording to Muhammad-bin-Ishaq and other historians, Adam(as) had 20 sons and 20 daughters. Some say that he begot 60 sons and 60 daughters. Then from them all the humans were born. The Taurah says that Adam(as) lived for 800 years after the birth of Seth. When Seth was born he was 130 years old. Then his other children were born. Adam(as) was 930 years old at the time of his death. (Genesis 5:1-5)\nAccording to some hadith, Adam(as) was 1000 years old. If this is to be accepted, maybe 70 years is the time which he spent in heaven. Before his death, Adam(as) appointed Seth as his representative and he was subsequently made a prophet by Allah(swt) and some book was also revealed to him. But there is no proof of this. Some scholars say that Adam(as) came down to the earth in India while some say that he was brought down in Mecca but there is no proof supporting either. His grave is supposed to be in India but there is no proof.\nThis is a brief biography of the first human being and also the first prophet. A year after he passed away, his wife Eve also died."],[18,"§Adan\n‘Adan’ means ‘always’, ‘forever’, ‘everlasting’. This word is used in the Holy Quran to describe the paradise; that it is forever and everlasting. Whoever enters it will never be made to leave it as it says in Surah Tauba:\n﴿وَعَدَ اللَّـهُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي مِن تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا وَمَسَاكِنَ طَيِّبَةً فِي جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ ۚ وَرِضْوَانٌ مِّنَ اللَّـهِ أَكْبَرُ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ ٧٢﴾\nAllah has promised the believing men and believing women gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide eternally, and pleasant dwellings in gardens of perpetual residence; but approval from Allah is greater. It is that which is the great attainment.\n[At-Tauba: 72]\nAnd the angels who bear the Throne will say to Allah(swt):\n﴿رَبَّنَا وَأَدْخِلْهُمْ جَنَّاتِ عَدْنٍ الَّتِي وَعَدتَّهُمْ وَمَن صَلَحَ مِنْ آبَائِهِمْ وَأَزْوَاجِهِمْ وَذُرِّيَّاتِهِمْ ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ ٨﴾\nOur Lord, and admit them to gardens of perpetual residence which You have promised them and whoever was righteous among their fathers, their spouses and their offspring. Indeed, it is You who is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\n[Al-Momin: 8]\nFor more information see Quran, Surah-16, An-Nahl, Verse-31; Surah-18, Al-Kahf, Verse-31; Surah-20, Ta-Ha, Verse-76 etc."],[19,"§Ahlul-Baith\nAhlul-Baith means the members of the house. Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّـهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا ٣٣﴾\nAllah(swt) intends only to remove from you the impurity [of sin], O people of the [Prophet's] household, and to purify you with [extensive] purification. [Al-Ahzab: 33]\nBased on the preceding and succeeding verses, we can conclude that the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) are being addressed here because they are the pillars on which the peace and honour of the house rests. Allah(swt) asks the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) to always be aware of whose wives they are and what duties they are bound to fulfill because He(swt) wants to remove forever all abomination from the house of the Holy Prophet(saws). Let us try to understand this in the light of the Holy Quran.\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ قُل لِّأَزْوَاجِكَ إِن كُنتُنَّ تُرِدْنَ الْحَيَاةَ الدُّنْيَا وَزِينَتَهَا فَتَعَالَيْنَ أُمَتِّعْكُنَّ وَأُسَرِّحْكُنَّ سَرَاحًا جَمِيلًا ٢٨ وَإِن كُنتُنَّ تُرِدْنَ اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَالدَّارَ الْآخِرَةَ فَإِنَّ اللَّـهَ أَعَدَّ لِلْمُحْسِنَاتِ مِنكُنَّ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا ٢٩ يَا نِسَاءَ النَّبِيِّ مَن يَأْتِ مِنكُنَّ بِفَاحِشَةٍ مُّبَيِّنَةٍ يُضَاعَفْ لَهَا الْعَذَابُ ضِعْفَيْنِ ۚ وَكَانَ ذَٰلِكَ عَلَى اللَّـهِ يَسِيرًا ٣٠ وَمَن يَقْنُتْ مِنكُنَّ لِلَّـهِ وَرَسُولِهِ وَتَعْمَلْ صَالِحًا نُّؤْتِهَا أَجْرَهَا مَرَّتَيْنِ وَأَعْتَدْنَا لَهَا رِزْقًا كَرِيمًا ٣١ يَا نِسَاءَ النَّبِيِّ لَسْتُنَّ كَأَحَدٍ مِّنَ النِّسَاءِ ۚ إِنِ اتَّقَيْتُنَّ فَلَا تَخْضَعْنَ بِالْقَوْلِ فَيَطْمَعَ الَّذِي فِي قَلْبِهِ مَرَضٌ وَقُلْنَ قَوْلًا مَّعْرُوفًا ٣٢ وَقَرْنَ فِي بُيُوتِكُنَّ وَلَا تَبَرَّجْنَ تَبَرُّجَ الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ الْأُولَىٰ ۖ وَأَقِمْنَ الصَّلَاةَ وَآتِينَ الزَّكَاةَ وَأَطِعْنَ اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ ۚ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّـهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا ٣٣﴾\nO Prophet, say to your wives, \"If you should desire the worldly life and its adornment, then come, I will provide for you and give you a gracious release. But if you should desire Allah(swt) and His Messenger(saws) and the home of the Hereafter - then indeed, Allah(swt) has prepared for the doers of good among you a great reward.\"\nO wives of the Prophet, whoever of you should commit a clear immorality - for her the punishment would be doubled two fold, and ever is that, for Allah(swt), easy.\nAnd whoever of you devoutly obeys Allah(swt) and His Messenger and does righteousness - We will give her her reward twice; and We have prepared for her a noble provision. O wives of the Prophet, you are not like anyone among women. If you fear Allah, then do not be soft in speech [to men], lest he in whose heart is disease should covet, but speak with appropriate speech. And abide in your houses and do not display yourselves as [was] the display of the former times of ignorance. And establish prayer and give zakah and obey Allah and His Messenger. Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity [of sin], O people of the [Prophet's] household, and to purify you with [extensive] purification.\n[Al-Ahzab: 28-33]\nIt is clearly understood from the above verses that ‘Ahlul-Baith’ means the honoured and pure wives of the Holy Prophet(saws) who are like the mothers of Muslims or ‘Ummul-Momineen’ about whom we should not entertain any dishonourable thought. It is for this reason that it was disallowed for them to remarry after the Holy Prophet(saws) passed away.\nIn the Holy Quran, the wives of Ibrahim(as) are also referred to as ‘Ahle-Baith’.\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿قَالُوا أَتَعْجَبِينَ مِنْ أَمْرِ اللَّـهِ ۖ رَحْمَتُ اللَّـهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ عَلَيْكُمْ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ ۚ إِنَّهُ حَمِيدٌ مَّجِيدٌ ٧٣﴾\nThey(the angels) said, \"Are you amazed at the decree of Allah? May the mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, people of the house. Indeed, He is Praiseworthy and Honorable.\" [Hud: 73]\nIn this verse ‘Ahle-Baith’ refers to Sara, the wife of Ibrahim(as). When she was given the good news that she would give birth to Ishaq(as), she expressed incredulity saying that it was not possible as she was barren and her husband was old.\nWe can conclude that first and foremost the word ‘Ahle-baith’ refers to the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nSecondly they refer to the progeny of the Holy Prophet(saws) as is evident from the following hadith:\n“Hazrat Aisha(ra) narrates that one day the Holy Prophet(saws) was seated with a woolen shawl wrapped around him. When his grandson Hasan-bin-Ali came up to him he(saws) wrapped him also in his shawl. Then his other grandson Hussain-bin-Ali also came up. The Holy Prophet(saws) wrapped the shawl around him too. Then his daughter Fatima came up and was wrapped up in the same way. Then his son-in-law Ali came up and was also taken in. Then the Holy Prophet(saws) recited the verse about ‘Ahle-Baith’”(Sahih Muslim: Fazail-e-Ahle-Baith)\nIn the same way Musnad Ahmad and Jamai Tirmizi quote some hadith that Fatima, the daughter of the Holy Prophet(saws), her husband Ali, and their sons Hasan and Hussain were ‘Ahle-Baith’. According to one hadith Umm-Salma, the pious wife of the Holy Prophet(saws) once asked him “Do I belong to Ahle-Baith?” To which the Holy Prophet(saws) replied, “You are one who does good deeds, you are from among my wives”. That is, you belong to the first level because this verse was revealed for my wives.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that ‘Ahle-Baith’ refers only to the wives of the Holy Prophet(saws).\nThirdly ‘Ahle-Baith’ refers to all the people who have been forbidden from accepting charity. This includes the progeny of Ali, Aqeel, Jaffer and Abbas as is narrated by Zaid-bin-Arkam in Sahih Muslim. But this is Zaid-bin-Arkam’s own conclusion regarding ‘Ahle-Baith’(Sahih Muslim: Fazail-e-Ali)\nIn the fourth place ‘Ahle-Baith’ also includes those people who are not related to the Holy Prophet(saws) in any way. For instance the Holy Prophet(saws) had said about Salman Farsi, “He is from among us” (Ibn-Zareer Tabri, 22:7)\nIn the same way he had said about Waasila-bin-Aska, “You are from among us”.\nWe can therefore conclude that ‘Ahle-Baith’ does not mean only Fatima, Ali and their sons Hasan and Hussain."],[20,"§Ahlul-Kitab\n‘Ahlul-Kitab’ are those people who possess and believe in some other book of revelation from Allah(swt) other than the Holy Quran. When the Holy Quran was revealed to Prophet Muhammad(saws), there were two kinds of people in the land of Arabia. To the first category belonged the people who did not have any book of revelation from Allah(swt). In the Holy Quran they are variously called as Kafirs(disbelievers), Mushrik(polytheists), Majoos(fire-worshippers), Saabii etc. To the second category belonged the people who did possess some book of revelation from Allah(swt), even though they had managed to distort the original version. The tribes belonging to this second category are referred to as ‘Ahlul Kitab’ or ‘Ahle-Kitab’ in the Holy Quran. The two main tribes of this category are the Jews and the Christians. For more information refer to ‘Jews’ and ‘Christians’.\nIn the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith, special instructions have been given about these two tribes. A few are discussed here.\nBelief of Ahle-Kitab:\nBoth the tribes claim to believe in Tawheed(Oneness of God), so in the Holy Quran they are being invited to the straight path of Tawheed.\n﴿قُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ تَعَالَوْا إِلَىٰ كَلِمَةٍ سَوَاءٍ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ أَلَّا نَعْبُدَ إِلَّا اللَّـهَ وَلَا نُشْرِكَ بِهِ شَيْئًا وَلَا يَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُنَا بَعْضًا أَرْبَابًا مِّن دُونِ اللَّـهِ ۚ فَإِن تَوَلَّوْا فَقُولُوا اشْهَدُوا بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ ٦٤﴾\nSay, \"O People of the Scripture, come to a word that is equitable between us and you - that we will not worship except Allah and not associate anything with Him and not take one another as lords instead of Allah.\" But if they turn away, then say, \"Bear witness that we are Muslims [submitting to Him].\"\n[Al-i-Imran: 64]\nThey are being invited towards the path of Tawheed because in spite of having the book of Allah(swt) with them, they had deviated towards shirk(polytheism) which would benefit them in no way.\n﴿وَقَالَتِ الْيَهُودُ عُزَيْرٌ ابْنُ اللَّـهِ وَقَالَتِ النَّصَارَى الْمَسِيحُ ابْنُ اللَّـهِ ۖ ذَٰلِكَ قَوْلُهُم بِأَفْوَاهِهِمْ ۖ يُضَاهِئُونَ قَوْلَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِن قَبْلُ ۚ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللَّـهُ ۚ أَنَّىٰ يُؤْفَكُونَ ٣٠﴾\nThe Jews say, \"Ezra is the son of Allah\"; and the Christians say, \"The Messiah is the son of Allah.\" That is their statement from their mouths; they imitate the saying of those who disbelieved [before them]. May Allah destroy them; how are they deluded?\n[At-Tawba: 30]\nJews believe Uzair(Ezra) to be the main person to cause the revival of their religion. According to their religious history, when Bukht Nasar, the king of Babylon destroyed the Baitul Muqaddas, burnt the Taurah and captured thousands of Jews and took them away to his country, the later generations not only became ignorant of their religion but also began forgetting their Hebrew language. It was then that the scholar named Uzair revived their religion. It is for this reason that the Jews started revering him and some even went so far as to call him the son of Allah(swt) (Inna AoozuBillah).\nSimilarly when the Christians saw that Isa(as) was born without a father, they made him the son of Allah(swt) (Inna AoozuBillah), made an image of him and started worshipping him. But Isa(as) never claimed divinity. To make their error manifest to them, Allah(swt) will ask Isa(as) on the Day of the Judgement:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ اللَّـهُ يَا عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ أَأَنتَ قُلْتَ لِلنَّاسِ اتَّخِذُونِي وَأُمِّيَ إِلَـٰهَيْنِ مِن دُونِ اللَّـهِ ۖ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ مَا يَكُونُ لِي أَنْ أَقُولَ مَا لَيْسَ لِي بِحَقٍّ ۚ إِن كُنتُ قُلْتُهُ فَقَدْ عَلِمْتَهُ ۚ تَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِي وَلَا أَعْلَمُ مَا فِي نَفْسِكَ ۚ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوبِ ١١٦﴾\nAnd [beware the Day] when Allah will say, \"O Jesus, Son of Mary, did you say to the people, 'Take me and my mother as deities besides Allah?'\" He will say, \"Exalted are You! It was not for me to say that to which I have no right. If I had said it, You would have known it. You know what is within myself, and I do not know what is within Yourself. Indeed, it is You who is Knower of the unseen.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 116]\nThat is Isa(as) will clearly deny that he ever instructed anybody to worship anyone besides Allah(swt).\nFood of Ahle-Kitab:\nMuslims are allowed to partake the food of Ahle-Kitab, including meat as long as it is not from a haram(unlawful) animal.\nالْيَوْمَ أُحِلَّ لَكُمُ الطَّيِّبَاتُ ۖ وَطَعَامُ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ حِلٌّ لَّكُمْ وَطَعَامُكُمْ حِلٌّ لَّهُمْ ۖ\nThis day [all] good foods have been made lawful, and the food of those who were given the Scripture is lawful for you and your food is lawful for them.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 5]\nMarrying the women of Ahle-Kitab has been made lawful for the Muslim men.\n﴿وَالْمُحْصَنَاتُ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنَاتِ وَالْمُحْصَنَاتُ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ مِن قَبْلِكُمْ إِذَا آتَيْتُمُوهُنَّ أُجُورَهُنَّ مُحْصِنِينَ غَيْرَ مُسَافِحِينَ وَلَا مُتَّخِذِي أَخْدَانٍ ۗ وَمَن يَكْفُرْ بِالْإِيمَانِ فَقَدْ حَبِطَ عَمَلُهُ وَهُوَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِينَ ٥﴾\nAnd [lawful in marriage are] chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those who were given the Scripture before you, when you have given them their due compensation, desiring chastity, not unlawful sexual intercourse or taking [secret] lovers. And whoever denies the faith - his work has become worthless, and he, in the Hereafter, will be among the losers.\n[Al-Ma’ida: 5]\nThere are some among Ahle-Kitab who perform righteous deeds:\n﴿لَيْسُوا سَوَاءً ۗ مِّنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ أُمَّةٌ قَائِمَةٌ يَتْلُونَ آيَاتِ اللَّـهِ آنَاءَ اللَّيْلِ وَهُمْ يَسْجُدُونَ ١١٣ يُؤْمِنُونَ بِاللَّـهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَيَأْمُرُونَ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ وَيَنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْمُنكَرِ وَيُسَارِعُونَ فِي الْخَيْرَاتِ وَأُولَـٰئِكَ مِنَ الصَّالِحِينَ ١١٤﴾\nThey are not [all] the same; among the People of the Scripture is a community standing [in obedience], reciting the verses of Allah during periods of the night and prostrating [in prayer]. They believe in Allah and the Last Day, and they enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong and hasten to good deeds. And those are among the righteous.\n[Al-i-Imran: 113-114]\nSome among Ahle-Kitab are trustworthy:\n﴿وَمِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ مَنْ إِن تَأْمَنْهُ بِقِنطَارٍ يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُم مَّنْ إِن تَأْمَنْهُ بِدِينَارٍ لَّا يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ إِلَّا مَا دُمْتَ عَلَيْهِ قَائِمًا ۗ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ قَالُوا لَيْسَ عَلَيْنَا فِي الْأُمِّيِّينَ سَبِيلٌ وَيَقُولُونَ عَلَى اللَّـهِ الْكَذِبَ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُونَ ٧٥﴾\nAnd among the People of the Scripture is he who, if you entrust him with a great amount [of wealth], he will return it to you. And among them is he who, if you entrust him with a [single] silver coin, he will not return it to you unless you are constantly standing over him [demanding it]. That is because they say, \"There is no blame upon us concerning the unlearned.\" And they speak untruth about Allah while they know [it].\n[Al-i-Imran: 75]\nThe Jews considered everybody other than themselves to be unlettered, that is the non-Jews were insignificant and so could be treated like animals. The wealth of others was lawful for the Jews and it was alright to even resort to falsehood to gain this wealth. That is why when Bani-Israel left Egypt, they did not return the wealth and things which had been entrusted to them by the Egyptians, even though Musa(as) never instructed them to do so.\nQuite contrary to this, when the Holy Prophet(saws) left Mecca for Madina, frustrated by the persecutions of the disbelievers, he left Ali(as) sleeping on his bed after instructing him to come to Madina only after returning all the things which had been entrusted to him, to their rightful owners. We Muslims take great pride in relating this story of our trustworthy Prophet Ameen(saws).\nSome of the people of ‘Ahle-Kitab’ believe in the Last Prophet(saws):\n﴿وَإِنَّ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ لَمَن يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّـهِ وَمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْكُمْ وَمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْهِمْ خَاشِعِينَ لِلَّـهِ لَا يَشْتَرُونَ بِآيَاتِ اللَّـهِ ثَمَنًا قَلِيلًا ۗ أُولَـٰئِكَ لَهُمْ أَجْرُهُمْ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ سَرِيعُ الْحِسَابِ ١٩٩﴾\nAnd indeed, among the People of the Scripture are those who believe in Allah and what was revealed to you and what was revealed to them, [being] humbly submissive to Allah. They do not exchange the verses of Allah for a small price. Those will have their reward with their Lord. Indeed, Allah is swift in account.\n[Al-i-Imran: 199]\n[See: Khamoos holy book (p.117) Isaiah(49:6) Romans(2:14) all refer to the others that is the non-Jews as unlettered. According to the second verse of the surah Al-Jumu’a, these people rejected the Last Prophet(saws):\n﴿هُوَ الَّذِي بَعَثَ فِي الْأُمِّيِّينَ رَسُولًا مِّنْهُمْ يَتْلُو عَلَيْهِمْ آيَاتِهِ وَيُزَكِّيهِمْ وَيُعَلِّمُهُمُ الْكِتَابَ وَالْحِكْمَةَ وَإِن كَانُوا مِن قَبْلُ لَفِي ضَلَالٍ مُّبِينٍ ٢﴾\nIt is He who has sent among the unlettered a Messenger from themselves reciting to them His verses and purifying them and teaching them the Book and wisdom - although they were before in clear error.\n[Al-Jumu’a: 2]\nOne translation of this verse is ‘Allah(swt) has sent a Prophet from the uneducated people’. Another meaning would be ‘Allah(swt) has sent a Prophet from among the non-Jews’. The Jews had settled in Madina waiting for the last Prophet who had been described in Taurah. But when he was raised up from among the uneducated non-Jews, they refused to believe in him though they recognized him by all the signs described in the Taurah.]"],[21,"§Al-Aama\n‘Al-Aama’ is the name of a Surah in the Holy Quran. Another name for this is ‘Abasa’. A blind person is described in this Surah, who used to live in Mecca. When the Holy Prophet(saws) had just started his propagation of Islam, this man had embraced Islam. Possibly, he hadn’t fully entered the fold of Islam, so he presented himself before the Messenger(saws) in order to gain more knowledge about Islam. The Holy Quran does not mention his name, but in the Sahih Hadith his name is given as Abdullah and his surname as ‘Ibn-Umme-Maqtoom’.\nIt so happened that on one occasion, the Holy Prophet(saws) was seated with some chieftains, to whom he was explaining Islam. Just then, this blind man approached him in order to ask something about Islam. This did not please the Holy Prophet(saws). Not because he(saws) did not sympathize with the weak and disabled, but because the chieftains who were with him considered themselves superior and the Holy Prophet(saws) feared lest they leave the assembly not wanting to mingle with the poor and the weak. He(saws) thought that if these leaders accepted Islam, its propagation would become much easier. So, this blind man’s coming to that elite assembly did not please him(saws). For more details refer to Tirmizi(5:432) and Ibn-Hibban(2:293, 535). The chain of this hadith is reliable. Allah(swt) was not pleased with this action of the Holy Prophet(saws) and He(swt) revealed the Surah ‘Abasa’ in which He(swt) expresses His displeasure. ‘Abasa’ means ‘to frown’.\nThe Prophet frowned and turned away. Because there came to him the blind man, [interrupting]. But what would make you perceive, [O Muhammad], that perhaps he might be purified. Or be reminded and the remembrance would benefit him? As for he who thinks himself without need, to him you give attention. And not upon you [is any blame] if he will not be purified. But as for he who came to you striving [for knowledge]. While he fears [Allah], from him you are distracted. No! Indeed, these verses are a reminder; so whoever wills may remember it.\n﴿عَبَسَ وَتَوَلَّىٰ ١ أَن جَاءَهُ الْأَعْمَىٰ ٢ وَمَا يُدْرِيكَ لَعَلَّهُ يَزَّكَّىٰ ٣ أَوْ يَذَّكَّرُ فَتَنفَعَهُ الذِّكْرَىٰ ٤ أَمَّا مَنِ اسْتَغْنَىٰ ٥ فَأَنتَ لَهُ تَصَدَّىٰ ٦ وَمَا عَلَيْكَ أَلَّا يَزَّكَّىٰ ٧ وَأَمَّا مَن جَاءَكَ يَسْعَىٰ ٨ وَهُوَ يَخْشَىٰ ٩ فَأَنتَ عَنْهُ تَلَهَّىٰ ١٠ كَلَّا إِنَّهَا تَذْكِرَةٌ ١١ فَمَن شَاءَ ذَكَرَهُ ١٢﴾\n[Abasa: 1-12]\nIt is said that many people entered the fold of Islam after reading these verses because they were convinced that this Quran was indeed from Allah(swt) because no other religion emphasizes the equality of all human beings – black or white, rich or poor."],[22,"§Al-Aarab\n‘Al-Aarab’ means the bedouins or the desert nomads who do not have a fixed place of living but are always moving from place to place with their cattle, sheep and camels. They erect their temporary tents wherever they find water and start staying there. All this rough living hardens them both physically and mentally. Due to lack of knowledge, they sometimes transgress the limits ordained by Allah(swt). At various places in the Holy Quran, this character of the bedouins has been described:\n﴿﴾ قَالَتِ الْأَعْرَابُ آمَنَّا ۖ قُل لَّمْ تُؤْمِنُوا وَلَـٰكِن قُولُوا أَسْلَمْنَا وَلَمَّا يَدْخُلِ الْإِيمَانُ فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ ۖ وَإِن تُطِيعُوا اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ لَا يَلِتْكُم مِّنْ أَعْمَالِكُمْ شَيْئًا ۚ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١٤﴾\nThe bedouins say, \"We have believed.\" Say, \"You have not [yet] believed; but say [instead], 'We have submitted,' for faith has not yet entered your hearts. And if you obey Allah and His Messenger, He will not deprive you from your deeds of anything. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\"\n[Al-Hujuraat: 14]\nThat is, these people simply claim to have believed, but the real faith has not fully entered their hearts. This external display of belief is being criticized as under in the Holy Quran:\n﴿الْأَعْرَابُ أَشَدُّ كُفْرًا وَنِفَاقًا وَأَجْدَرُ أَلَّا يَعْلَمُوا حُدُودَ مَا أَنزَلَ اللَّـهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ٩٧﴾\nThe bedouins are stronger in disbelief and hypocrisy and more likely not to know the limits of what [laws] Allah has revealed to His Messenger. And Allah is Knowing and Wise.\n[At-Tawba: 97]\n﴿وَمِمَّنْ حَوْلَكُم مِّنَ الْأَعْرَابِ مُنَافِقُونَ ۖ وَمِنْ أَهْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ ۖ مَرَدُوا عَلَى النِّفَاقِ لَا تَعْلَمُهُمْ ۖ نَحْنُ نَعْلَمُهُمْ ۚ سَنُعَذِّبُهُم مَّرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّونَ إِلَىٰ عَذَابٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٠١﴾\nAnd among those around you of the bedouins are hypocrites, and [also] from the people of Madinah. They have become accustomed to hypocrisy. You, [O Muhammad], do not know them, [but] We know them. We will punish them twice [in this world]; then they will be returned to a great punishment.\n[At-Tawba: 101]\n﴿سَيَقُولُ لَكَ الْمُخَلَّفُونَ مِنَ الْأَعْرَابِ شَغَلَتْنَا أَمْوَالُنَا وَأَهْلُونَا فَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ۚ يَقُولُونَ بِأَلْسِنَتِهِم مَّا لَيْسَ فِي قُلُوبِهِمْ ۚ قُلْ فَمَن يَمْلِكُ لَكُم مِّنَ اللَّـهِ شَيْئًا إِنْ أَرَادَ بِكُمْ ضَرًّا أَوْ أَرَادَ بِكُمْ نَفْعًا ۚ بَلْ كَانَ اللَّـهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرًا ١١﴾\nThose who remained behind of the bedouins will say to you, \"Our properties and our families occupied us, so ask forgiveness for us.\" They say with their tongues what is not within their hearts. Say, \"Then who could prevent Allah at all if He intended for you harm or intended for you benefit? Rather, ever is Allah, with what you do, Acquainted.\n[Al-Fath: 11]\nIn this verse the reference is to that Umra of the Holy Prophet(saws), whose declaration he had made before the victory over Mecca. The Bedouins thought that the people of Mecca who were baying for the blood of the Muslims would surely kill all of them. So, it would be suicidal to go there and hence they did not accompany the Holy Prophet(saws) (See ‘Hudaibiya’). But among these Bedouins were some who were true Muslims.\n﴿وَمِنَ الْأَعْرَابِ مَن يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّـهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْآخِرِ وَيَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنفِقُ قُرُبَاتٍ عِندَ اللَّـهِ وَصَلَوَاتِ الرَّسُولِ ۚ أَلَا إِنَّهَا قُرْبَةٌ لَّهُمْ ۚ سَيُدْخِلُهُمُ اللَّـهُ فِي رَحْمَتِهِ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّـهَ غَفُورٌ رَّحِيمٌ ٩٩﴾\nBut among the bedouins are some who believe in Allah and the Last Day and consider what they spend as means of nearness to Allah and of [obtaining] invocations of the Messenger. Unquestionably, it is a means of nearness for them. Allah will admit them to His mercy. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful.\n[At-Tawba: 99]"],[23,"§Al-Ahqaf\nAhqaf is the plural of ‘Hiqf’ which means big pebbles of mud. ‘Al-Ahqaf’ is a Surah of the Holy Quran and it consists of 35 Verses. ‘Ahqaf’ is described in the 21st Verse of this Surah:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ أَخَا عَادٍ إِذْ أَنذَرَ قَوْمَهُ بِالْأَحْقَافِ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ النُّذُرُ مِن بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِ أَلَّا تَعْبُدُوا إِلَّا اللَّـهَ إِنِّي أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ٢١﴾\nAnd mention, [O Muhammad], the brother of 'Aad, when he warned his people in the [region of] al-Ahqaf - and warners had already passed on before him and after him - [saying], \"Do not worship except Allah. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a terrible day.\" [Al-Ahqaf: 21]\n‘Ahqaf’ here refers to a desert region situated to the south of Saudi Arabia. It is known as ‘Rubaa Khaali’. Once upon a time this place was inhabited by a very big tribe by the name of ‘Aad’. A few signs and traces of this civilization can still be seen today at a place called ’Hajar Maut’. Hud(as) was sent as a prophet to this tribe. But the people of Aad did not pay heed to his teachings as a result of which a terrible storm totally wiped out the entire tribe.\n﴿وَفِي عَادٍ إِذْ أَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الرِّيحَ الْعَقِيمَ ٤١ مَا تَذَرُ مِن شَيْءٍ أَتَتْ عَلَيْهِ إِلَّا جَعَلَتْهُ كَالرَّمِيمِ ٤٢﴾\nAnd in 'Aad [was a sign], when We sent against them the barren wind. It left nothing of what it came upon but that it made it like disintegrated ruins. [Adh-Dhariyat: 41, 42]\nFurther explanation is given in the following verses:\n﴿كَذَّبَتْ عَادٌ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ ١٨ إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا صَرْصَرًا فِي يَوْمِ نَحْسٍ مُّسْتَمِرٍّ ١٩ تَنزِعُ النَّاسَ كَأَنَّهُمْ أَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ مُّنقَعِرٍ ٢٠﴾\n'Aad denied; and how [severe] were My punishment and warning. Indeed, We sent upon them a screaming wind on a day of continuous misfortune, Extracting the people as if they were trunks of palm trees uprooted.\n[Al-Qamar: 18, 20]\nIt says in the Holy Quran that this storm lasted for seven nights and eight days as a result of which everything was ruined.\n﴿فَهَلْ تَرَىٰ لَهُم مِّن بَاقِيَةٍ ٨﴾\nThen do you see of them any remains? [Al-Haqqa: 8]\nHence, Surah-Ahqaf describes the terrible consequences of not following Allah’s(swt) teachings, taking the example of the tribe of ‘Aad’. ‘Aad’ which was a very great tribe of those times was completely annihilated for going against the orders of Allah(swt). We should learn from this that any country or tribe, however powerful and great, is nothing before the All-Powerful Lord of this entire creation and He(swt) has the power to reduce it to dust should it dare to go against His decrees.\nFor further details about ‘Aad’ refer to ‘Hud’."],[24,"§Al-Asr\nAl-Asr is the name of a Surah in the Holy Quran which means ‘passage of time’. It has a total of three verses whose translation is as follows:\n﴿وَالْعَصْرِ ١ إِنَّ الْإِنسَانَ لَفِي خُسْرٍ ٢ إِلَّا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا بِالصَّبْرِ ٣﴾\nBy time, Indeed, mankind is in loss, Except for those who have believed and done righteous deeds and advised each other to truth and advised each other to patience.\n[Al-Asr: 1-3]\nThis Surah was revealed in Mecca when Islam was in its initial stages. This Surah is basically addressed to those who invite people to the true straight path. The people who do not believe in Allah(swt) and the Holy Prophet(saws) and refrain from doing righteous deeds are truly the losers. And moreover it is not easy to convince them about the message of Allah(swt) namely the Holy Quran. So, lots of courage and patience is required for this task of making the people take note of what is being said and save themselves from a great loss.\n‘Asr’ is also the obligatory salah offered between the Zuhur and Magrib salahs. In the Sahih Hadith, this salah has been given great importance.\n“Whoever misses his Asr salah is like the one who has lost his family and his wealth.”\n(Refer :Bukhari, 552, Muslim, 200)\n“Whoever misses his Asr salah, all his good will be annulled.”\n(Refer : Bukhari, 553)"],[25,"§Alcohol\nThe Holy Quran has forbidden alcohol forever. Islam advocates the safety of five things: safety of life, safety of wealth, safety of chastity, safety of dignity, and safety of good sense. Going against these entails severe punishment. For the safety of good sense it is necessary for alcohol to be banned forever. But in the country where the Holy Quran was revealed, drinking alcohol was widely prevalent. So, it was a very difficult task to ban alcohol in one go. First the following verses were revealed:\nيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ ۖ قُلْ فِيهِمَا إِثْمٌ كَبِيرٌ وَمَنَافِعُ لِلنَّاسِ وَإِثْمُهُمَا أَكْبَرُ مِن نَّفْعِهِمَا ۗ\nThey ask you about wine and gambling. Say, \"In them is great sin and [yet, some] benefit for people. But their sin is greater than their benefit.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 219]\nThis was the first step in which the bad consequences of alcohol were mentioned. A few wise people began guessing that maybe alcohol would be completely forbidden. Then the following verses were revealed:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَقْرَبُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَأَنتُمْ سُكَارَىٰ حَتَّىٰ تَعْلَمُوا مَا تَقُولُونَ وَلَا جُنُبًا إِلَّا عَابِرِي سَبِيلٍ حَتَّىٰ تَغْتَسِلُوا ۚ ﴾\nO you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying or in a state of janabah, except those passing through [a place of prayer], until you have washed [your whole body].\n[An-Nisa: 43]\nThat is, people who consumed alcohol were forbidden from offering salah. Then the following verses were revealed:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْأَنصَابُ وَالْأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٩٠ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَاءَ فِي الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَن ذِكْرِ اللَّـهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلَاةِ ۖ فَهَلْ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١﴾\nO you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through intoxicants and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?\n[Al-Ma’ida: 90-91]\nAs soon as these verses were revealed, people emptied all the wine and wine containers and wine started flowing like water through the streets of Madina. People gave up drinking forever. This is a clear miracle of Allah(swt) and the Holy Quran that the tribe who were used to drinking at every step of their life gave it up completely at a moment’s notice.\nToday alcohol and gambling are the terrible diseases afflicting the so-called cultured societies and the wise people want to rid the society of these monsters. But Islam is the only religion which offers a permanent solution to this malaise. Many countries have propounded many laws to overcome this but to no avail."],[26,"§Alif-Laam-Meem\nMany of the Surahs of the Holy Quran have this type of letters occurring at the beginning of the Surah, which are called ‘Huroof-e-Mukhta’aat’ in Arabic. This means separate letters. There is a difference of opinion regarding this among the scholars. Some scholars say that these are the names of the Surahs which have ‘Huroof-e-Mukhta’aat’ at their beginning. For example Surah-20, Ta-Ha; Surah-36, Yasin;Surah-38, Saad; Surah-50, Qaf; but some Surahs which have ‘Huroof-e-Mukhta’aat’ occurring at their beginning are not referred to by them. For example:\nAlif-Laam-Meem:\nSurah-2, Al-Baqara; Surah-3, Al-i-Imran;Surah-29, Al-Ankaboot; Surah-30, Ar-Rum; Surah-31,Luqman; Surah-32, As-Sajdah.\nAlif-Laam-Meem-Saad:\nSurah-7,Al-Araf\nAlif-Laam-Raa:\nSurah-10, Yunus;Surah-11,Hud; Surah-12,Yusuf;Surah-13, Ar-Raad;Surah-14,Ibrahim; Surah-15, Al-Hijr.\nKaaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Saad:\nSurah-19, Maryam.\nTa-Seen-Meem:\nSurah-26, Ash-Shu’ara; Surah-27,An-Naml;Surah-28, Al-Qasas.\nHa-Meem:\nSurah-40, Momin; Surah-41, Fussilat; Surah-43, Az-Zukhruf; Surah-44,Ad-Dukhan;Surah-45,Al-Jathiya; Surah-46, Al-Ahqaf.\nHa-Meem-Ayn-Seen-Qaf:\nSurah-42,Ash-Shura.\nNoon:\nSurah-68, Al-Qalam.\nSome scholars are of the opinion that by using ‘Huroof-e-Mukhta’aat’ Allah(swt) has challenged the Arabic poets and authors that I have sent down the Holy Quran which uses letters with which you are quite familiar. If any of you have any doubts regarding this, produce a similar book, if not the entire book produce at least a surah, if not an entire surah produce at least a verse. It is one of the miracles of the Holy Quran that no one has taken up the challenge to date.\nA few scholars are of the opinion that just as in the Chinese language various pictures can be joined to convey a variety of meanings which is called an ‘ideogram’, these letters may also have some meaning which can be found in the surah at the beginning of which these letters occur. They base their opinion on the records found during the Egyptian excavations in which pictures have been used to depict letters. For example Ta-Ha means snake and in Surah-20,Ta-ha, in the story of Musa(as), reference is made to a snake. Similar researches have been done by the Indian scholars Moulana Hamidduddin Farahi and Moulana Abul-Jalal Nadvi. But much more needs to be done. But these researches are not really important for understanding the Holy Quran.\nSome scholars feel that these letters are abbreviations of some words and these type of short forms are common in the Arabic language.\nSome scholars say that the true knowledge of these letters is with Allah(swt) alone and that He(swt) is testing us whether we are believers or not because not knowing the meaning of these ‘Huroof-e-Mukhta’aat’ is not a hindrance for understanding the Holy Quran.\nWe cannot conclusively say as to which is the correct version but it is true that this style of descriptive writing was very popular in those times. That is the reason why though many aspects of the Holy Quran were criticized, no fault was found with the ‘Huroof-e-Mukhta’aat’. This clearly means that in those times people were familiar with this style of writing. Otherwise the critics would definitely have posed the question as to what sort of a book is this in which it is difficult to understand even the names of the surahs; when the Holy Quran is undoubtedly ‘Kitab-e-Mubeen’ meaning that every word in it is crystal clear."],[27,"§Al-i-Imran\nAl-i-Imran means the offspring of Imran. Al-i-Imran is the name of the third surah of the Holy Quran. The word ‘Al-i-Imran’ is used in the thirty-third verse of this surah whose translation is as follows:\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ اصْطَفَىٰ آدَمَ وَنُوحًا وَآلَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَآلَ عِمْرَانَ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ ٣٣﴾\nIndeed, Allah chose Adam and Noah and the family of Abraham and the family of 'Imran over the worlds.\n[Al-i-Imran: 33]\nIn the history of Bani-Israel there were two people named Imran. One was the father of Musa(as) and Haroon(as) who is mentioned in Exodus(6:20) as Amram. The other was the father of Maryam who is mentioned as ‘Imran’ in the Holy Quran.(Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-35 ). It is not surprising that the Holy Bible does not mention the name of the father of Maryam because the life of Isa(as) himself is given very briefly. It is only the final book of revelation, the Holy Quran that describes Isa(as) as a true slave of Allah(swt).\n﴿إِنَّ اللَّـهَ اصْطَفَىٰ آدَمَ وَنُوحًا وَآلَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَآلَ عِمْرَانَ عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ ٣٣ ذُرِّيَّةً بَعْضُهَا مِن بَعْضٍ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ ٣٤ إِذْ قَالَتِ امْرَأَتُ عِمْرَانَ رَبِّ إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِي بَطْنِي مُحَرَّرًا فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّي ۖ إِنَّكَ أَنتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ ٣٥﴾\nNow the question arises as to who is the person referred to in the Surah Al-i-Imran – the father of Musa(as) and Haroon(as) or the father of Maryam? It can be understood from Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-35, that the person is the father of Maryam because Allah(swt) had chosen Isa(as) for the people of this world and sent him as a messenger to the Bani-Israel. He was not the son of Allah(swt) but all these people were the descendants from one another as is clear from Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-34.\nIn the same verse it is mentioned that Allah(swt) is ‘the Hearing and the Knowing’. That is if you give a prophet or messenger some other status, then be warned that Allah(swt) hears and knows everything and will definitely question you about it."],[28,"§Allah’s rope (hold fast the rope of Allah(swt))\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nوَاعْتَصِمُوا بِحَبْلِ اللَّـهِ جَمِيعًا وَلَا تَفَرَّقُوا ﴾\nAnd hold firmly to the rope of Allah all together and do not become divided. [Al-Imran: 103]\nWhat is meant by the ‘rope of Allah(swt)’ is the teachings of the Holy Quran and the Holy Prophet(saws) because these two are the main springs of Islam and a true Muslim is the one who is steadfast in following what is prescribed therein. The Holy Prophet(saws) says in his last sermon “I am leaving behind two things, the Holy Quran and my example, Sunnah. Anybody who sincerely follows these shall never go astray.”\nProving this the above verse continues:\nوَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ كُنتُمْ أَعْدَاءً فَأَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِكُمْ فَأَصْبَحْتُم بِنِعْمَتِهِ إِخْوَانًا وَكُنتُمْ عَلَىٰ شَفَا حُفْرَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ فَأَنقَذَكُم مِّنْهَا ۗ كَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ آيَاتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ\nAnd remember the favor of Allah upon you - when you were enemies and He brought your hearts together and you became, by His favor, brothers. And you were on the edge of a pit of the Fire, and He saved you from it. Thus does Allah make clear to you His verses that you may be guided.\nOnly by holding fast the rope of Allah(swt), the two tribes of Madina, ‘Ous’ and ‘Khajraj’ who were previously enemies were joined by brotherly love which was nothing short of a miracle. This revelation should teach us Muslims not to fight over petty issues and sow mischief among ourselves but grasp firmly the Holy Quran and Sunnah and continuously thank the Almighty for the innumerable favours which He(swt) in His infinite mercy has bestowed upon us."],[29,"§Altars\nGoing to the altars for worshipping, asking favours, offering gifts and food, prostrating etc. are strictly forbidden in Islam. Sometimes the object of worship may be an idol or sometimes it may be the grave of some pious person. The foolish people blindly go to these places for worshipping and asking favours when the only One who can benefit or harm them is Allah(swt) alone and not the dead people or false gods and goddesses. And this goes against the main theme of Islam namely ‘Tawheed’ or monotheism. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالْأَنصَابُ وَالْأَزْلَامُ رِجْسٌ مِّنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ فَاجْتَنِبُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ ٩٠ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَن يُوقِعَ بَيْنَكُمُ الْعَدَاوَةَ وَالْبَغْضَاءَ فِي الْخَمْرِ وَالْمَيْسِرِ وَيَصُدَّكُمْ عَن ذِكْرِ اللَّـهِ وَعَنِ الصَّلَاةِ ۖ فَهَلْ أَنتُم مُّنتَهُونَ ٩١﴾\nO you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it that you may be successful. Satan only wants to cause between you animosity and hatred through intoxicants and gambling and to avert you from the remembrance of Allah and from prayer. So will you not desist?\n[Al-Ma’ida: 90-91]\nAccording to Musnad Ahmad(2:351) when this verse was revealed, the Muslims said, “O Lord! We have reformed.”\nSo, the people who call themselves Muslims but practice many blind customs and biddat are far far away from the teachings of Islam. It is imperative for them to understand the real meaning of Tawheed and make it an integral part of their lives."],[30,"§Alwah\nAlwah is the plural of ‘Lauh’ which means ‘plaque’, ‘tablet’, ‘plank’ or ‘slate’ which can be used for writing. The word ‘Alwah’ is used in the Holy Quran in three contexts:\nWhen Nuh(as) built the ark to escape the great flood it is mentioned that the ark was built using planks and iron nails:\n﴿وَحَمَلْنَاهُ عَلَىٰ ذَاتِ أَلْوَاحٍ وَدُسُرٍ ١٣﴾\nAnd We carried him on a [construction of] planks and nails [Al-Qamar: 13]\nThe word is used with regard to the place where the original Holy Quran is preserved namely ‘Lauh-e-Mehfooz’\n﴿بَلْ هُوَ قُرْآنٌ مَّجِيدٌ ٢١ فِي لَوْحٍ مَّحْفُوظٍ ٢٢﴾\nBut this is an honored Qur'an [Inscribed] in a Preserved Slate. [Al-Buruj: 21-22].\nThat is why it is impossible for mortals to make any change in the Holy Quran. And that is why any copy of the Holy Quran from any corner of the world has the exact words which were revealed to the Holy Prophet(saws). Where is this ‘Lauh-e-Mehfooz’? We can understand from the Holy Quran that it is near the throne of Allah(swt) where no living being can go.\nIt is also used for the tablets which were given by Allah(swt) to Musa(as):\n﴿وَكَتَبْنَا لَهُ فِي الْأَلْوَاحِ مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ مَّوْعِظَةً وَتَفْصِيلًا لِّكُلِّ شَيْءٍ فَخُذْهَا بِقُوَّةٍ وَأْمُرْ قَوْمَكَ يَأْخُذُوا بِأَحْسَنِهَا ۚ سَأُرِيكُمْ دَارَ الْفَاسِقِينَ ١٤٥﴾\nAnd We wrote for him on the tablets [something] of all things - instruction and explanation for all things, [saying], \"Take them with determination and order your people to take the best of it. I will show you the home of the defiantly disobedient.\"\n[Al-Aaraf: 145]\nWhen Musa(as) returned from the mountain to his tribe to preach to them what Allah(swt) had taught him, he found the tribe of Bani-Israel worshipping the calf which they had built with their own hands while he had clear instructions forbidding idol-worship.(refer: Bible,Exodus, 32:15-20).So, Musa was very angry and threw the tablets to one side.\n﴿وَلَمَّا رَجَعَ مُوسَىٰ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ غَضْبَانَ أَسِفًا قَالَ بِئْسَمَا خَلَفْتُمُونِي مِن بَعْدِي ۖ أَعَجِلْتُمْ أَمْرَ رَبِّكُمْ ۖ وَأَلْقَى الْأَلْوَاحَ وَأَخَذَ بِرَأْسِ أَخِيهِ يَجُرُّهُ إِلَيْهِ ۚ قَالَ ابْنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ الْقَوْمَ اسْتَضْعَفُونِي وَكَادُوا يَقْتُلُونَنِي فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِيَ الْأَعْدَاءَ وَلَا تَجْعَلْنِي مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ ١٥٠﴾\nAnd when Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved, he said, \"How wretched is that by which you have replaced me after [my departure]. Were you impatient over the matter of your Lord?\" And he threw down the tablets and seized his brother by [the hair of] his head, pulling him toward him. [Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, indeed the people oppressed me and were about to kill me, so let not the enemies rejoice over me and do not place me among the wrongdoing people.\" [Al-Aaraf: 150]\nHe questioned his brother Haroon(as) as to why they had resorted to idol-worship.\n﴿وَلَمَّا سَكَتَ عَن مُّوسَى الْغَضَبُ أَخَذَ الْأَلْوَاحَ ۖ وَفِي نُسْخَتِهَا هُدًى وَرَحْمَةٌ لِّلَّذِينَ هُمْ لِرَبِّهِمْ يَرْهَبُونَ ١٥٤﴾\nAnd when the anger subsided in Moses, he took up the tablets; and in their inscription was guidance and mercy for those who are fearful of their Lord.\n[Al-Aaraf: 154]\nAccording to the Holy Quran and the Holy Bible whatever was written on these tablets was written by Allah(swt) Himself.\nAccording to the Holy Bible:\nThe LORD said to Moses, “Come up to me on the mountain and stay here, and I will give you the tablets of stone with the law and commandments I have written for their instruction.”\n(Bible,Exodus, 24:12 )\nThere is no mention in the Holy Quran whether the tablets broke or not when Musa(as) threw them aside in anger but according to the Holy Bible they did break.\nThe LORD said to Moses, “Chisel out two stone tablets like the first ones, and I will write on them the words that were on the first tablets, which you broke.\n(Bible, 34:1)\nSo Moses chiseled out two stone tablets like the first ones and went up Mount Sinai early in the morning, as the LORD had commanded him; and he carried the two stone tablets in his hands.\n(Bible,34:4)\nWe can deduce from the Holy Quran that when Musa(as) threw the tablets aside and then picked them up they could have been broken. Later they could have been joined and the contents noted. They could have been freshly copied onto other tablets later on. The writers of the Bible have written this in another way.\nWhat was written on those tablets?\nIt is written in the Holy Quran that those tablets contained teachings about every aspect of life; that is, what is necessary in their religion.\nReligion is based on two main things: Faith and Actions. According to the Holy Bible those tablets had the Ten Commandments.\nMoses was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights without eating bread or drinking water. And he wrote on the tablets the words of the covenant—the Ten Commandments.\n(Bible, 34:28) and these are about faith and actions. Now let us study these Ten Commandments.\nFaith:\n1. And God spoke all these words:\n“I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.Bible(20:1-2)\n2. You shall have no other gods before me.\n“You shall not make for yourself an image in the form of anything in heaven above or on the earth beneath or in the waters below. 5 You shall not bow down to them or worship them; for I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God, punishing the children for the sin of the parents to the third and fourth generation of those who hate me, 6 but showing love to a thousand generations of those who love me and keep my commandments.\n“You shall not misuse the name of the LORD your God, for the LORD will not hold anyone guiltless who misuses his name. Bible(20:3-7)\nActions:\n3. “Remember the Sabbath day by keeping it holy. 9Six days you shall labor and do all your work, 10but the seventh day is a sabbath to the LORD your God. On it you shall not do any work, neither you, nor your son or daughter, nor your male or female servant, nor your animals, nor any foreigner residing in your towns. 11For in six days the LORD made the heavens and the earth, the sea, and all that is in them, but he rested on the seventh day. Therefore the LORD blessed the Sabbath day and made it holy.Bible(20:8-11)\n4. “Honor your father and your mother, so that you may live long in the land the LORD your God is giving you.Bible(20:12)\n5. You shall not murder.\n6. You shall not commit adultery.\n7. You shall not steal.\n8. You shall not give false testimony against your neighbor.\n9. You shall not covet your neighbor’s house.\n10. You shall not covet your neighbor’s wife, or his male or female servant, his ox or donkey, or anything that belongs to your neighbor.” Bible(20:13-17)\nThe Bible elaborates about these commandments at other places as well. For instance, forbidding idol-worship, it says:\nBe careful not to make a treaty with those who live in the land where you are going, or they will be a snare among you. Break down their altars, smash their sacred stones and cut down their Asherah poles. Do not worship any other god, for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God.\n(Bible,Exodus,34:12-14)\nThis makes it clear that what was revealed to Musa(as) was the same as that revealed to all the other prophets(as) and to the last prophet Hazrath Muhammad(saws). That is the concept of ‘One God’. Just as the other prophets forbade idol-worship so did Musa(as). This proves that basically all the prophets were taught the same thing namely ‘to worship one God’. As regards the other teachings they continued to change with time.\nImportant note: The word ‘Yehova’ occurs often in the Taurah. ‘Yehova’ is the name by which the Jews call Allah(swt). But they consider it a sin to speak out this word. So they use the word ‘Adonai’ instead, which means ‘My Lord’ in Hebrew. According to the Jewish teachings, only once during the year, on a special day this word can be used on the talisman of Sulaiman(as). That is the reason why they have formed a word called tetragram (a word forming four letters) in the Greek language. They use this word instead of ‘Yehova’ because ‘Yehova’ consists of four letters in the Hebrew language.\nThe Holy Bible says in the Exodus:\nMoses said to God, “Suppose I go to the Israelites and say to them, ‘The God of your fathers has sent me to you,’ and they ask me, ‘What is his name?’ Then what shall I tell them?”\nGod said to Moses, “I AM WHO I AM. This is what you are to say to the Israelites: ‘I AM has sent me to you.’”(Bible,Exodus,3:13-14)\nReferring to this teaching of the Jews, Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nقُلِ ادْعُوا اللَّـهَ أَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمَـٰنَ ۖ أَيًّا مَّا تَدْعُوا فَلَهُ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ ۚ ﴾\nSay, \"Call upon Allah or call upon the Most Merciful. Whichever [name] you call - to Him belong the best names.\" [Bani-Israel: 110]\n﴿وَلِلَّـهِ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ فَادْعُوهُ بِهَا ۖ وَذَرُوا الَّذِينَ يُلْحِدُونَ فِي أَسْمَائِهِ ۚ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ١٨٠﴾\nAnd to Allah belong the best names, so invoke Him by them. And leave [the company of] those who practice deviation concerning His names. They will be recompensed for what they have been doing.[Al-Araf: 180]"],[31,"§Al-Yasa(Elisha)\nProphet Al-Yasa(as) is mentioned in two places in the Holy Quran. In the first instance Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَالْيَسَعَ وَيُونُسَ وَلُوطًا ۚ وَكُلًّا فَضَّلْنَا عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ ٨٦﴾\nAnd Ishmael and Elisha and Jonah and Lot - and all [of them] We preferred over the worlds. [Al-An’am: 86]\nIn the preceding verse the Holy Quran mentions Prophet Ibraheem(as). Then after referring to his descendants Ishaq, Yaqub, Zachariah, Yahya, Isa and Ilyas(as) mention is made of Ismael, Al-Yasa, Yunus and Lut(as). This proves that Al-Yasa(as) was from among the progeny of Ibraheem(as). Some scholars have traced the roots of Al-Yasa(as) in the following way: Al-Yasa son of Aswat, son of Di, son of Sholtam, son of Akraeem, son of Yusuf, son of Yakub, son of Ishaq, son of Ibraheem(as).\nIn the second instance Prophet Al-Yasa(as) is described in the Holy Quran as follows:\n﴿وَاذْكُرْ إِسْمَاعِيلَ وَالْيَسَعَ وَذَا الْكِفْلِ ۖ وَكُلٌّ مِّنَ الْأَخْيَارِ ٤٨﴾\nAnd remember Ishmael, Elisha and Dhul-Kifl, and all are among the outstanding.\n[Saad: 48]\nEven here in the preceding verse, Prophet Ibraheem(as) is being described. It says that Ibraheem, Ishaq and Yaqub(as) were among the chosen ones. After them Ishmael, Al-Yasa and Dhul-Kifl(as) are mentioned. So we understand that all of them were the chosen ones of Allah(swt).\nAccording to Hasan Basri, a renowned scholar, Al-Yasa(as) was a contemporary of Ilyas(as) and after Ilyas(as), Al-Yasa(as) called the people towards the path of Allah(swt). (Refer to Ibn-Kasir, Khisse-Anbiya P.472).\nTherefore it is possible that he must be the Yasa bin Shaft mentioned in the Bible who was born in a village of Jordan. His father was very wealthy. One day when Al-Yasa was going to the fields, Prophet Ilyas(as) happened to pass by him and he put his shawl over him. Then, Al-Yasa(as) followed him and started staying with him and started propagating Islam. After the demise of Ilyas(as), he continued working for the Bani-Israel. He lived from 878 to 838 B.C. The Holy Bible describes many of his miracles, the most popular among them being the revival of the dead son of a Shunnamite lady( Refer to 2 Kings 4:8-37). Al-Yasa(as) died and was buried. After a year the Moabite raiders entered the country. Once when some Israelites were burying a man, they suddenly saw a band of raiders; so they threw the man’s body into Al-Yasa’s(as) tomb. When the body touched Al-Yasa’s(as) bones, the man came to life and stood up on his feet (Refer to 2 Kings 13:20-21).\nAs there is no confirmation about these miracles either in the Holy Quran or the Sahih Hadith, we cannot comment on them because according to Sahih Hadith we should neither confirm nor reject the sayings of ‘Ahle Kitab’."],[32,"§Anfal\nAnfal is the plural of ‘Nafl’. It means ‘more’ or ‘extra’ or ‘excess’. When somebody is given something which is more than what is due, the excess quantity is called ‘Nafl’. Similarly when a person does more than what is compulsory, the extra work is called ‘Nafl’.\nThat is why the salah other than the five compulsory salahs are called ‘Nafl’ salah.\nAl-Anfal is the name of the eighth surah of the Holy Quran which was revealed after the Battle of Badr of 2 A.H. This was the first war between the Muslims and the disbelievers in which the Muslims emerged victorious and collected a lot of war-booty. Now the question arose as to who should get this war-booty; the persons who collected them or the persons involved in the various activities of war? Or was it haram for them? Because before the advent of the Prophet(saws) there were no specific rules regarding the spoils of war. Sometimes whoever collected something would keep it or sometimes the leader of the group was the sole owner of all the gains. It was a rule of some tribes that they collected the war-booty and then the lightning would strike it and turn all of it to ashes as it was haram. So, according to a hadith, the Prophet(saws) says:\n“The war-booty has been made halal for me, for the tribes before me it was not halal.”\n(Bukhari,438,Muslim,521)\nThe Prophet(saws) wanted to know about the division of this halal war-booty. Explanation is given in Surah-Anfal:\n﴿يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْأَنفَالِ ۖ قُلِ الْأَنفَالُ لِلَّـهِ وَالرَّسُولِ ۖ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ وَأَصْلِحُوا ذَاتَ بَيْنِكُمْ ۖ وَأَطِيعُوا اللَّـهَ وَرَسُولَهُ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤْمِنِينَ ١﴾\nThey ask you, [O Muhammad], about the bounties [of war]. Say, \"The [decision concerning] bounties is for Allah and the Messenger.\" So fear Allah and amend that which is between you and obey Allah and His Messenger, if you should be believers.\n[Al-Anfal: 1]\nAfter this, the subsequent verses contain many instructions for the Muslims. Then in the 41st verse, the answer to the question posed in the 1st verse is answered thus:\n﴿وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّمَا غَنِمْتُم مِّن شَيْءٍ فَأَنَّ لِلَّـهِ خُمُسَهُ وَلِلرَّسُولِ وَلِذِي الْقُرْبَىٰ وَالْيَتَامَىٰ وَالْمَسَاكِينِ وَابْنِ السَّبِيلِ إِن كُنتُمْ آمَنتُم بِاللَّـهِ وَمَا أَنزَلْنَا عَلَىٰ عَبْدِنَا يَوْمَ الْفُرْقَانِ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ٤١﴾\nAnd know that anything you obtain of war booty - then indeed, for Allah is one fifth of it and for the Messenger and for [his] near relatives and the orphans, the needy, and the [stranded] traveler, if you have believed in Allah and in that which We sent down to Our Servant on the day of criterion - the day when the two armies met. And Allah, over all things, is competent.\n[Al-Anfal: 41]\nThe explanation of this is as follows. The war-booty is to be divided into five equal portions; four of which are to be divided among the soldiers. The fifth portion is to be deposited in the government treasury. This portion would again be divided into five equal parts. One portion would be for Allah(swt) and His Prophet(saws) which the Prophet(saws) would utilize for himself and for the service of the community. After the Prophet(saws) this portion would go to the Khalifa who would use it for the community. The second portion would be for the Prophet(saws)’s family and his close aides. The third portion was to be used for the orphans, the fourth for the poor and the fifth for the wayfarer or traveler. This would be at the discretion of the Prophet(saws) or the ruler of the Muslims after him according to the needs of the people.\nThe rules of war and peace enunciated in the Surah-8,Al-Anfal of the Holy Quran are the best to date. So it is imperative to study this Surah in detail and glean the gems of wisdom from it."],[33,"§Angels\nThe Holy Quran refers to the angels as ‘Malaaika’ which is the plural form of ‘Malak’. Belief in the angels is one of the main beliefs in Islam as is mentioned in the Holy Quran:\nكُلٌّ آمَنَ بِاللَّـهِ وَمَلَائِكَتِهِ وَكُتُبِهِ وَرُسُلِهِ\nAll of them have believed in Allah and His angels and His books and His messengers.\n[Al-Baqara: 285]\nThe angels have been described in various places in the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith from which we understand that they are creatures whom Allah(swt) has created from light and then allocated various tasks for them. For example every human has two angels allocated to him who note down all his good and bad deeds.\n﴿إِذْ يَتَلَقَّى الْمُتَلَقِّيَانِ عَنِ الْيَمِينِ وَعَنِ الشِّمَالِ قَعِيدٌ ١٧﴾\nWhen the two receivers receive, seated on the right and on the left. Man does not utter any word except that with him is an observer prepared [to record].\n[Qaf: 17]\nIn the same way some angels have been given the task of taking out the souls of men, some are for questioning the dead in the graves etc. Whatever is happening around us in this universe is being performed by the angels fulfilling the commands of Allah(swt):\n﴿لَّا يَعْصُونَ اللَّـهَ مَا أَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُونَ مَا يُؤْمَرُونَ ٦﴾\nThey do not disobey Allah in what He commands them but do what they are commanded.\n[At-Tahrim: 6]\nIt is mandatory for us to believe in the angels but worshipping them or considering them to be gods and goddesses is forbidden. The angels take care of matters pertaining to our lives but do only what is commanded by Allah(swt). Only Allah(swt) is worthy of worship, Who is governing His creation with the help of the angels. These are the angels whom the polytheists mistakenly believe to be their intercessors with Allah(swt) and end up worshipping them. Based on their imagination they have even made their idols and prostrate before them. In the same way many other tribes have also done what the polytheists of Arabia have done. The angels have been described in the Holy Quran using various names. For example:\nRasool: This means a messenger:\nالْحَمْدُ لِلَّـهِ فَاطِرِ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ جَاعِلِ الْمَلَائِكَةِ رُسُلًا أُولِي أَجْنِحَةٍ مَّثْنَىٰ وَثُلَاثَ وَرُبَاعَ ۚ\n[All] praise is [due] to Allah, Creator of the heavens and the earth, [who] made the angels messengers having wings, two or three or four.\n[Fatir: 1]\nSafara:\nThis is the plural of ‘Saafir’ which is used for a scribe and reader.[Abasa: 15]. From this word is derived ‘Safeer’ which is used for angels. This angel performs the task of smoothening the affairs between Allah(swt) and His creation. According to one sahih hadith:\n“Anyone who recites the Holy Quran and also memorises it will be like ‘Safrah Kiraam ba-ra-rah.’”\n(Sahih Bukhari:4937 and Sahih Muslim:798)\nThat is he will be like the angels who are esteemed, honored and steadfast in their devotion.\nMost of the scholars are of the opinion that in the Holy Quran, ‘Safrah Kiraam ba-ra-rah’ means angels.\nJunood:\nThis is the plural of ‘Jundi’ which means army. At various places in the Holy Quran, the word ‘Junood’ has been used for angels. The Holy Quran says:\nيَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اذْكُرُوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّـهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ جَاءَتْكُمْ جُنُودٌ فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ رِيحًا وَجُنُودًا لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا ۚ ﴾\nO you who have believed, remember the favor of Allah upon you when armies came to [attack] you and We sent upon them a wind and armies [of angels] you did not see.\n[Al-Ahzab: 9]\nHere what is meant by the armies which were not seen are the angels who were sent down from the heavens for helping the Muslims against the disbelievers in the battle of Khandakh. It is described in the Sahih Hadith that the enemies were falling down from their horses but the creatures who were making them fall were not being seen. In the same way, the Holy Quran says in Surah-9, At-Tawba, Verse-26:\nثُمَّ أَنزَلَ اللَّـهُ سَكِينَتَهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِ وَعَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَأَنزَلَ جُنُودًا لَّمْ تَرَوْهَا\nThen Allah sent down His tranquillity upon His Messenger and upon the believers and sent down soldiers angels whom you did not see.\nMala’i-Aala:\nThe word ‘Mala’i-Aala’ has been used for the angels which means the most exalted assembly of angels:\n﴿لَّا يَسَّمَّعُونَ إِلَى الْمَلَإِ الْأَعْلَىٰ وَيُقْذَفُونَ مِن كُلِّ جَانِبٍ ٨﴾\n[So] they may not listen to the exalted assembly [of angels] and are pelted from every side.\n[Al-Saffat: 8]\n﴿مَا كَانَ لِيَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ بِالْمَلَإِ الْأَعْلَىٰ إِذْ يَخْتَصِمُونَ ٦٩﴾\nI had no knowledge of the exalted assembly [of angels] when they were disputing [the creation of Adam].\n[Saad: 69]\nOther than these a few other words have also been used for the angels which are not very popular."],[34,"§Anger\nThe Holy Quran uses the word ‘Gazab’ for anger. It means anger, fury, curse etc. This includes both the ‘Gazab’ of Allah(swt) as well as that of people. The anger of Allah(swt) is used for the reform of humans. (See Surah-48, Al-Fath, Verse-60; Surah-6, Al-Mumtahina, Verse-13; Surah-24, An-Noor, Verse-9)\nBut the anger of men is against the teachings of Islam.\nThat is why the person who controls his anger is being praised in the Holy Quran.\n﴿الَّذِينَ يُنفِقُونَ فِي السَّرَّاءِ وَالضَّرَّاءِ وَالْكَاظِمِينَ الْغَيْظَ وَالْعَافِينَ عَنِ النَّاسِ ۗ وَاللَّـهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ ١٣٤﴾\nWho spend [in the cause of Allah] during ease and hardship and who restrain anger and who pardon the people - and Allah loves the doers of good.\n[Al-i-Imran: 134]\nAccording to the sahih hadith, the truly strong person is the one who when angry, restrains himself. (See Bukhari, 6114 and Muslim, 2609)\nAccording to a sahih hadith a person came up to the Holy Prophet(saws) and asked him for some good advice. The Holy Prophet(saws) told him, “Control your anger.” The person again requested him for some more good advice. The Holy Prophet(saws) again preached the same thing. In this way the person kept requesting the Holy Prophet(saws) to preach him something and the Holy Prophet(saws) kept preaching. “Control your anger.” ( Sahih Bukhari, 6116)\nAnd the Holy Prophet(saws) himself would not get angry as long as the commands of Allah(swt) were being carried out. But when somebody was disobedient to Allah(swt), he(saws) would be furious."],[35,"§Ansar\nAnsar is the plural of ‘Nasir’ which means ‘helpers’.\nMadina was inhabited by both Arabs and the Jews. The Arabs belonged to the two tribes ‘Ous’ and ‘Khajraj’. It seems that during the second century A.D. these tribes had migrated from Yemen and settled here and were continuously at war with each other. Islam united these two warring tribes and joined them in the bond of brotherhood.\nReferring to this Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَاعْتَصِمُوا بِحَبْلِ اللَّـهِ جَمِيعًا وَلَا تَفَرَّقُوا ۚ وَاذْكُرُوا نِعْمَتَ اللَّـهِ عَلَيْكُمْ إِذْ كُنتُمْ أَعْدَاءً فَأَلَّفَ بَيْنَ قُلُوبِكُمْ فَأَصْبَحْتُم بِنِعْمَتِهِ إِخْوَانًا وَكُنتُمْ عَلَىٰ شَفَا حُفْرَةٍ مِّنَ النَّارِ فَأَنقَذَكُم مِّنْهَا ۗ كَذَٰلِكَ يُبَيِّنُ اللَّـهُ لَكُمْ آيَاتِهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ ١٠٣﴾\nAnd hold firmly to the rope of Allah all together and do not become divided. And remember the favor of Allah upon you - when you were enemies and He brought your hearts together and you became, by His favor, brothers. And you were on the edge of a pit of the Fire, and He saved you from it. Thus does Allah make clear to you His verses that you may be guided. [Al-Imran: 103]\nThese two tribes ‘Ous’ and ‘Khajraj’ and the Jews who accepted Islam are together called Ansar.\nWhen Isa(as) sought help from his tribe, his disciples said:\n﴿فَلَمَّا أَحَسَّ عِيسَىٰ مِنْهُمُ الْكُفْرَ قَالَ مَنْ أَنصَارِي إِلَى اللَّـهِ ۖ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنصَارُ اللَّـهِ آمَنَّا بِاللَّـهِ وَاشْهَدْ بِأَنَّا مُسْلِمُونَ ٥٢﴾\nBut when Jesus felt [persistence in] disbelief from them, he said, \"Who are my supporters for [the cause of] Allah?\" The disciples said, \"We are supporters for Allah. We have believed in Allah and testify that we are Muslims [submitting to Him].\n[Al-Imran: 52]\nAllah(swt) commands the Muslims:\n﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُونُوا أَنصَارَ اللَّـهِ كَمَا قَالَ عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ لِلْحَوَارِيِّينَ مَنْ أَنصَارِي إِلَى اللَّـهِ ۖ قَالَ الْحَوَارِيُّونَ نَحْنُ أَنصَارُ اللَّـهِ ۖ فَآمَنَت طَّائِفَةٌ مِّن بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ وَكَفَرَت طَّائِفَةٌ ۖ فَأَيَّدْنَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا عَلَىٰ عَدُوِّهِمْ فَأَصْبَحُوا ظَاهِرِينَ ١٤﴾\nO you who have believed, be supporters of Allah, as when Jesus, the son of Mary, said to the disciples, \"Who are my supporters for Allah?\" The disciples said, \"We are supporters of Allah.\" And a faction of the Children of Israel believed and a faction disbelieved. So We supported those who believed against their enemy, and they became dominant.[Al-Saff: 14]\nThen this word started being used only for the inhabitants of Madina because the way in which they helped their brothers who had migrated from Mecca(Muhajir) was such that its parallel cannot be found in history. Consider the following example:\nNabi(saws) made Abdur-Rehman-bin-Ouf(Muhajir) a brother of Saad-bin-Rabii(Ansari). Saad said to Abdur-Rehman, “Brother, I have abundant wealth. Take one half of it. In the same way you may marry one of my two wives after I divorce her and the period of waiting(iddat) is over”. Abdur-Rehman replied, “May Allah increase your wealth and family. Just show me the way to the market”. Then, he went into business and did very well. Very soon he also married an Ansar lady.(Sahih-Bukhari, 3780)\nFor this reason Allah(swt) has given glad tidings to both the immigrants and Ansar in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَالسَّابِقُونَ الْأَوَّلُونَ مِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنصَارِ وَالَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُم بِإِحْسَانٍ رَّضِيَ اللَّـهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوا عَنْهُ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُمْ جَنَّاتٍ تَجْرِي تَحْتَهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا أَبَدًا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ الْفَوْزُ الْعَظِيمُ ١٠٠﴾\nAnd the first forerunners [in the faith] among the Muhajireen and the Ansar and those who followed them with good conduct - Allah is pleased with them and they are pleased with Him, and He has prepared for them gardens beneath which rivers flow, wherein they will abide forever. That is the great attainment.\n[At-Tauba: 100]\n﴿لَّقَد تَّابَ اللَّـهُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالْأَنصَارِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِن بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٍ مِّنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ ۚ إِنَّهُ بِهِمْ رَءُوفٌ رَّحِيمٌ ١١٧﴾\nAllah has already forgiven the Prophet and the Muhajireen and the Ansar who followed him in the hour of difficulty after the hearts of a party of them had almost inclined [to doubt], and then He forgave them. Indeed, He was to them Kind and Merciful.\n[At-Tauba: 117]\nAfter praising the immigrants, the Ansar are being praised in the following verses:\n﴿وَالَّذِينَ تَبَوَّءُوا الدَّارَ وَالْإِيمَانَ مِن قَبْلِهِمْ يُحِبُّونَ مَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَيْهِمْ وَلَا يَجِدُونَ فِي صُدُورِهِمْ حَاجَةً مِّمَّا أُوتُوا وَيُؤْثِرُونَ عَلَىٰ أَنفُسِهِمْ وَلَوْ كَانَ بِهِمْ خَصَاصَةٌ ۚ وَمَن يُوقَ شُحَّ نَفْسِهِ فَأُولَـٰئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُونَ ٩﴾\nAnd [also for] those who were settled in al-Madinah and [adopted] the faith before them. They love those who emigrated to them and find not any want in their breasts of what the emigrants were given but give [them] preference over themselves, even though they are in privation. And whoever is protected from the stinginess of his soul - it is those who will be the successful.\n[Al-Hashr: 9]\nNabi(saws) has also heaped praise on the Ansar. According to a hadith Nabi(saws) has said:\n“I shall pass through the same valley through which the Ansar pass. If there had been no migration I would have liked to be from among the Ansar.”\n(Bukhari,3779)\nOnce when the Ansar brothers requested the Prophet(saws) to distribute their date fields among their immigrant brothers, the Prophet(saws) replied:\n“No, you tend to your farms, but while harvesting include them in sharing the harvest.”\n(Bukhari,3782)\nThe reason why the Prophet(saws) replied thus was because the immigrants did not know farming and if they’d been given the fields, the harvest would be definitely low. On the other hand they were very good in trade and commerce. It was the Prophet(saws)’s desire that Madina should also flourish like Mecca and become a prominent trade centre. In another hadith the Prophet(saws) says:\n“A Momin(believer) will love an Ansar while a hypocrite will hate an Ansar. So, Allah(swt) will love him who loves an Ansar and will hate him who hates an Ansar.”\n(Bukhari, 3783 and Muslim,75)\nThe service to the cause of Islam and its propagation worldwide by the Ansar brothers is exemplary. That is the reason why they were so beloved to the Prophet(saws). After the victory over Mecca, they were anxious thinking that the Prophet(saws) would return to Mecca. But the Prophet(saws) stayed on in Madina till his last breath and was finally laid to rest there itself."],[36,"§Ant\nAn ant is one of the weakest of the insects. But from ancient times it has been used as an example of hard work, wisdom and activeness. It is wise because in places where the winters are severe and there is nothing to be found for eating, the ants gather and store enough food during summer itself.\nThe Holy Quran has a surah named ‘Naml’ which means ‘ant’. It has a total of 93 verses. It was revealed in Mecca. In its 18th verse, ‘naml’ is described three times. And from this too the wisdom of the ants is obvious.\nAllah(swt) has made the jinn, men and birds subservient to Sulaiman(as):\n﴿حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَتَوْا عَلَىٰ وَادِ النَّمْلِ قَالَتْ نَمْلَةٌ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّمْلُ ادْخُلُوا مَسَاكِنَكُمْ لَا يَحْطِمَنَّكُمْ سُلَيْمَانُ وَجُنُودُهُ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ ١٨﴾\nUntil, when they came upon the valley of the ants, an ant said, \"O ants, enter your dwellings that you not be crushed by Solomon and his soldiers while they perceive not.\"\n[An-Naml: 18]"],[37,"§Arabic\nArabic is the best and most ancient of all the languages of the world. The Holy Quran was revealed in Arabic. Historians believe that Arabic was used as early as 2000 B.C. Ismail(as), the son of Ibrahim(as) also used this language because his wife’s tribe who were related to the ‘Jurham’ group of Yemen used Arabic.\nThe ancient tribes of Arab Tasm, Judais and first Aad tribes etc. used Arabic only. Some scholars are of the opinion that Arabic is the mother of Hebrew, Aramaic, Ashuri, Finiki etc. languages. That is why these languages have many words in common with Arabic. But a few other scholars say that these are all sister-languages as they are as ancient as Arabic. But as to which is the mother-language, nobody is certain. Some western scholars are of the opinion that the mother-language is the Sami language and Arabic is the closest to the Sami languages as many words and rules of grammar are common to Arabic and the Sami languages.\nDuring the revelation of the Holy Quran, Arabic language was at its zenith. In the market place of a place called ‘Ukaaz’ in Mecca, many Arabic poets and linguistic scholars would assemble and recite their poetry. But on hearing the Arabic of the Holy Quran, they were awe-struck because till then they had prided themselves on being the best. On hearing the sweet, refined and embellished Arabic in which the Holy Quran was being revealed to the unlettered Prophet(saws), they were stunned. Referring to this, the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَلَقَدْ نَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُمْ يَقُولُونَ إِنَّمَا يُعَلِّمُهُ بَشَرٌ ۗ لِّسَانُ الَّذِي يُلْحِدُونَ إِلَيْهِ أَعْجَمِيٌّ وَهَـٰذَا لِسَانٌ عَرَبِيٌّ مُّبِينٌ ١٠٣﴾\nAnd We certainly know that they say, \"It is only a human being who teaches the Prophet.\" The tongue of the one they refer to is foreign, and this Qur'an is [in] a clear Arabic language.\n[An-Nahl: 103]\nThat is why it is declared in the Holy Quran that these are not the words of any human but the teachings of the All-Powerful Allah(swt):\n﴿وَإِنَّهُ لَتَنزِيلُ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ١٩٢ نَزَلَ بِهِ الرُّوحُ الْأَمِينُ ١٩٣ عَلَىٰ قَلْبِكَ لِتَكُونَ مِنَ الْمُنذِرِينَ ١٩٤ بِلِسَانٍ عَرَبِيٍّ مُّبِينٍ ١٩٥ وَإِنَّهُ لَفِي زُبُرِ الْأَوَّلِينَ ١٩٦﴾\nAnd indeed, the Qur'an is the revelation of the Lord of the worlds. The Trustworthy Spirit has brought it down. Upon your heart, [O Muhammad] - that you may be of the warners - In a clear Arabic language. And indeed, it is [mentioned] in the scriptures of former peoples.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 192-196]\n﴿وَلَقَدْ ضَرَبْنَا لِلنَّاسِ فِي هَـٰذَا الْقُرْآنِ مِن كُلِّ مَثَلٍ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٢٧ قُرْآنًا عَرَبِيًّا غَيْرَ ذِي عِوَجٍ لَّعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُونَ ٢٨﴾\nAnd We have certainly presented for the people in this Qur'an from every [kind of] example - that they might remember. [It is] an Arabic Qur'an, without any deviance that they might become righteous.\n[Az-Zumar: 27-28]\nThe Holy Prophet(saws) conveyed the message to the people in Arabic. He(saws) was uneducated, but still spoke a sweet and refined Arabic. In fact, he(saws) once declared “I speak the best Arabic among all the Arabs”. The same Arabic which was used in the Holy Quran and Sahih Hadith is still in use all over the world.\nThe rules of grammar for Arabic were written when Islam had spread beyond the Arab countries to places where Arabic was not used. Abul Aswad Dulvi (expired 79 A.H.) was the first person who wrote the rules of grammar. After him Abdullah bin Ishaq Hajrami (expired 117 A.H.), Isa bin Umar Saqfi (expired 149 A.H.) and Abu Umr bin Ala (expired 154 A.H.) wrote books on Arabic grammar. The most famous book was ‘Al-Kitab’ written by Seebvyh (expired 180 A.H.).\nAbout this time many books were written to make Arabic easy to learn especially for people whose mother tongue was not Arabic. Popular among them are:\n‘Annahawul Wazeh’ by Ali Zarim and Mustafa.\n‘Jam-e-Durus Arbiyah’ by Mustafa Galayani.\n‘Duroosul-Lughtul Arbiyah’ by the famous Indian Arabic scholar Dr. F. Abdur-Raheem, which was first published by the Madina University has now been published by India, Pakistan, Turkey, England, Korea, Russia, America etc.\nArabic can be learnt very easily. Today in many countries like India, Pakistan etc. where Arabic is not spoken, it is being taught in their Islamic centres. It is one of the miracles of the Holy Quran that the Arabic language hasn’t undergone any change down the ages while all other languages change every couple of years and finally die down."],[38,"§Arafat\nArafat is an open area which lies about 22 kilometers to the east of Mecca. It is described only once in the Holy Quran:\n﴿لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَن تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلًا مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ ۚ فَإِذَا أَفَضْتُم مِّنْ عَرَفَاتٍ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّـهَ عِندَ الْمَشْعَرِ الْحَرَامِ ۖ وَاذْكُرُوهُ كَمَا هَدَاكُمْ وَإِن كُنتُم مِّن قَبْلِهِ لَمِنَ الضَّالِّينَ ١٩٨﴾\nThere is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord [during Hajj]. But when you depart from 'Arafat, remember Allah at al- Mash'ar al-Haram. And remember Him, as He has guided you, for indeed, you were before that among those astray.\n[Al-Baqara: 198]\nThis is the same where during the Haj, the pilgrim has to stay from morning till evening. Here the Zuhur and the Asr salahs are combined. It is obligatory to stay at Arafat during the prescribed period without which Haj is null and void. That is why according to a Sahih Hadith, the Holy Prophet(saws) has said:\n“Haj is Arafat.”\n‘Arafat’ is derived from ‘Arafa’ which means ‘to know’ or ‘recognise’. According to a hadith of Ibn-Abbas, Jibrail(as) taught the rules of Haj to Ibraheem(as) at this place. So, it was named ‘Arafa’.\nIn Arafat is the small hillock which is called ‘Jable-Rehmat’. It is here that during the Haj, the Holy Prophet(saws) delivered his famous last sermon. The meanings found in this sermon are indeed astounding, touching upon some of the most important rights God has over humanity, and humanity has over each other. It is considered as the first declaration of human rights. After preaching the sermon, he retired to his tent and that is the place where ‘Masjid-e-Namira’ stands today. The Saudi Government rebuilt the mosque lavishly. It has 64 doorways and a capacity of about three and a half lakh. It also houses one thousand rest rooms and fifteen thousand ablution places."],[39,"§Arsh\nIn the Holy Quran, ‘Arsh’ is used in two contexts:\nIn the first context it means the roof of a house. As when Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿أَوْ كَالَّذِي مَرَّ عَلَىٰ قَرْيَةٍ وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَىٰ عُرُوشِهَا قَالَ أَنَّىٰ يُحْيِي هَـٰذِهِ اللَّـهُ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا ۖ فَأَمَاتَهُ اللَّـهُ مِائَةَ عَامٍ ثُمَّ بَعَثَهُ ۖ قَالَ كَمْ لَبِثْتَ ۖ قَالَ لَبِثْتُ يَوْمًا أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ ۖ قَالَ بَل لَّبِثْتَ مِائَةَ عَامٍ فَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ طَعَامِكَ وَشَرَابِكَ لَمْ يَتَسَنَّهْ ۖ وَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ حِمَارِكَ وَلِنَجْعَلَكَ آيَةً لِّلنَّاسِ ۖ وَانظُرْ إِلَى الْعِظَامِ كَيْفَ نُنشِزُهَا ثُمَّ نَكْسُوهَا لَحْمًا ۚ فَلَمَّا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ قَالَ أَعْلَمُ أَنَّ اللَّـهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ قَدِيرٌ ٢٥٩﴾\nOr [consider such an example] as the one who passed by a township which had fallen into ruin. He said, \"How will Allah bring this to life after its death?\" So Allah caused him to die for a hundred years; then He revived him. He said, \"How long have you remained?\" The man said, \"I have remained a day or part of a day.\" He said, \"Rather, you have remained one hundred years. Look at your food and your drink; it has not changed with time. And look at your donkey; and We will make you a sign for the people. And look at the bones [of this donkey] - how We raise them and then We cover them with flesh.\" And when it became clear to him, he said, \"I know that Allah is over all things competent.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 259]\nSome scholars are of the opinion that the reference here is to Prophet Ezekiel.\nIn the second context it means ‘throne’. In the Holy Quran, the Hud-Hud bird speaks to Hazrat Sulaiman(as) as:\n﴿إِنِّي وَجَدتُّ امْرَأَةً تَمْلِكُهُمْ وَأُوتِيَتْ مِن كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيمٌ ٢٣﴾\nIndeed, I found [there] a woman ruling them, and she has been given of all things, and she has a great throne.\n[An-Naml: 23]\nThe word ‘Arsh’ is also used for the ‘Throne of Allah(swt)’ as in the Holy Quran:\n﴿اللَّـهُ لَا إِلَـٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ ۩ ٢٦﴾\nAllah - there is no deity except Him, Lord of the Great Throne.\n[An-Naml: 26]\n‘Lord of the Great Throne’ means that Allah(swt) is its Creator and it is a thing which the angels carry:\n﴿الَّذِينَ يَحْمِلُونَ الْعَرْشَ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهُ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَيُؤْمِنُونَ بِهِ وَيَسْتَغْفِرُونَ لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا رَبَّنَا وَسِعْتَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ رَّحْمَةً وَعِلْمًا فَاغْفِرْ لِلَّذِينَ تَابُوا وَاتَّبَعُوا سَبِيلَكَ وَقِهِمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيمِ ٧﴾\nThose [angels] who carry the Throne and those around it exalt [Allah] with praise of their Lord and believe in Him and ask forgiveness for those who have believed, [saying], \"Our Lord, You have encompassed all things in mercy and knowledge, so forgive those who have repented and followed Your way and protect them from the punishment of Hellfire.\n[Al-Momin: 7]\n﴿وَالْمَلَكُ عَلَىٰ أَرْجَائِهَا ۚ وَيَحْمِلُ عَرْشَ رَبِّكَ فَوْقَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ ثَمَانِيَةٌ ١٧﴾\nAnd the angels are at its edges. And there will bear the Throne of your Lord above them, that Day, eight [of them].\n[Al-Haqqa: 17]\nIt is said that these angels who bear the Throne would be very strong. It would take seven hundred years to traverse the distance between their shoulder and ear. (Refer Abu Dawood, 4727)\nThe Throne of Allah(swt) is the greatest and loftiest creation. The entire Creation is like a small hole in a desert in its comparison. According to a Sahih Bukhari hadith:\nIf you want to ask something from Allah(swt) ask for the paradise named Firdaus because that is the loftiest station in paradise. And along with it is the ‘Arsh’ of Allah(swt) from where the rivers of the paradise originate.”\n(Sahih Bukhari, 7423)\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَهُوَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٍ وَكَانَ عَرْشُهُ عَلَى الْمَاءِ لِيَبْلُوَكُمْ أَيُّكُمْ أَحْسَنُ عَمَلًا ۗ وَلَئِن قُلْتَ إِنَّكُم مَّبْعُوثُونَ مِن بَعْدِ الْمَوْتِ لَيَقُولَنَّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا إِنْ هَـٰذَا إِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِينٌ ٧﴾\nAnd it is He who created the heavens and the earth in six days - and His Throne had been upon water - that He might test you as to which of you is best in deed. But if you say, \"Indeed, you are resurrected after death,\" those who disbelieve will surely say, \"This is not but obvious magic.\"\n[Hud: 7]\nFrom the above verse, it is obvious that the Throne is a thing and that it has been created by Allah(swt) and then He(swt) ascended it. Our knowledge about this is very less because our mental faculties are limited while Allah(swt) is the Possessor of unlimited knowledge and wisdom. A limited entity cannot encompass something which is beyond its scope. That is why, believing in the unseen, we just accept whatever the verses of the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith tell us about the Throne(Arsh). We try not to entertain disquieting thoughts. This has been the policy of the pious companions of the Holy Prophet(saws) and religious scholars."],[40,"§Asbaat\n‘Asbaat’ is the plural of ‘Sibt’. This means ‘dynasty’ or ‘family’. In the Holy Quran, the offspring of Yaqub(as) are referred to as ‘Asbaat’.\n﴿قُولُوا آمَنَّا بِاللَّـهِ وَمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَيْنَا وَمَا أُنزِلَ إِلَىٰ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْمَاعِيلَ وَإِسْحَاقَ وَيَعْقُوبَ وَالْأَسْبَاطِ وَمَا أُوتِيَ مُوسَىٰ وَعِيسَىٰ وَمَا أُوتِيَ النَّبِيُّونَ مِن رَّبِّهِمْ لَا نُفَرِّقُ بَيْنَ أَحَدٍ مِّنْهُمْ وَنَحْنُ لَهُ مُسْلِمُونَ ١٣٦﴾\nSay, [O believers], \"We have believed in Allah and what has been revealed to us and what has been revealed to Abraham and Ishmael and Isaac and Jacob and the Descendants and what was given to Moses and Jesus and what was given to the prophets from their Lord. We make no distinction between any of them, and we are Muslims [in submission] to Him.\"\n[Al-Baqara: 136]\nSimilarly refer to Surah-3, Al-i-Imran, Verse-84 and Surah-4, An-Nisa, Verse-163. Then the word was used for a sub-group among Jews just as the word Kabeela(tribe) was used for Arabs. As in:\n﴿وَمِن قَوْمِ مُوسَىٰ أُمَّةٌ يَهْدُونَ بِالْحَقِّ وَبِهِ يَعْدِلُونَ ١٥٩ وَقَطَّعْنَاهُمُ اثْنَتَيْ عَشْرَةَ أَسْبَاطًا أُمَمًا ۚ وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ إِذِ اسْتَسْقَاهُ قَوْمُهُ أَنِ اضْرِب بِّعَصَاكَ الْحَجَرَ ۖ فَانبَجَسَتْ مِنْهُ اثْنَتَا عَشْرَةَ عَيْنًا ۖ قَدْ عَلِمَ كُلُّ أُنَاسٍ مَّشْرَبَهُمْ ۚ وَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الْغَمَامَ وَأَنزَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَىٰ ۖ كُلُوا مِن طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ ۚ وَمَا ظَلَمُونَا وَلَـٰكِن كَانُوا أَنفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُونَ ١٦٠﴾\nAnd among the people of Moses is a community which guides by truth and by it establishes justice. And We divided them into twelve descendant tribes [as distinct] nations. And We inspired to Moses when his people implored him for water, \"Strike with your staff the stone,\" and there gushed forth from it twelve springs. Every people knew its watering place. And We shaded them with clouds and sent down upon them manna and quails, [saying], \"Eat from the good things with which We have provided you.\" And they wronged Us not, but they were [only] wronging themselves.\n[Al-A’raf: 159-160]\nAccording to the Holy Bible, the twelve sons of Yaqub(as) were called ‘Asbaat’:\n1. Reuben 2. Simeon 3. Levi 4. Judah 5. Dan 6. Napthali 7. Gad 8. Asher\n9. Issachar 10. Zebulun 11. Joseph 12. Benjamin.\nOf these, instead of Levi and Joseph, the sons of Joseph, ‘Afraeem’ and ‘Mansi’ were elected. The son of Levi was made the priest of Haikal(house of worship). These twelve ‘Asbat’ were together till the time of Sulaiman(as). Each ‘sibt’ had a chieftain. After the demise of Sulaiman(as), all these tribes fought among themselves and the kingdom of Bani-Israel was divided into two parts. Just as there were twelve ‘Asbaat’ in Israel, Isa(as) sent twelve messengers to spread his message and teachings to Bani-Israel. This proves that Isa’s(as) call was for the Jews and not for the entire world."],[41,"§Asma-e-husna\nThis means the most beautiful and holy names of Allah(swt).\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَلِلَّـهِ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ فَادْعُوهُ بِهَا ۖ وَذَرُوا الَّذِينَ يُلْحِدُونَ فِي أَسْمَائِهِ ۚ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ١٨٠﴾\nAnd to Allah belong the best names, so invoke Him by them. And leave [the company of] those who practice deviation concerning His names. They will be recompensed for what they have been doing. [Al-Araf: 180]\nAsma-e-husna can be useful in two ways:\nFirstly we can worship Allah(swt) using them. For instance we can beseech Allah(swt) saying “Oh Forgiver of sins please forgive me” or “Oh Most Merciful One please have mercy on me” or “Oh Giver of Livelihood please grant me livelihood” etc. Using these names Allah(swt) and none other should be worshipped. None other than Allah(swt) should be given these names nor addressed using them.\nSecondly we should worship Allah(swt) according to these names. For instance we should seek His forgiveness because He(swt) alone accepts His slaves’ forgiveness. We prostrate before Him because He(swt) is the Greatest and He(swt) has no partner in His Greatness. We Muslims prostrate before Him every day during our salah because Allah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَمِنْ آيَاتِهِ اللَّيْلُ وَالنَّهَارُ وَالشَّمْسُ وَالْقَمَرُ ۚ لَا تَسْجُدُوا لِلشَّمْسِ وَلَا لِلْقَمَرِ وَاسْجُدُوا لِلَّـهِ الَّذِي خَلَقَهُنَّ إِن كُنتُمْ إِيَّاهُ تَعْبُدُونَ ٣٧﴾\nAnd of His signs are the night and day and the sun and moon. Do not prostrate to the sun or to the moon, but prostrate to Allah, who created them, if it should be Him that you worship.\n[Ha-Meem As-Sajdah: 37]\n﴿وَمِنَ اللَّيْلِ فَاسْجُدْ لَهُ وَسَبِّحْهُ لَيْلًا طَوِيلًا ٢٦﴾\nAnd during the night prostrate to Him and exalt Him a long [part of the] night. [Ad-Dahr: 26]\nAccording to Sahih hadith, Allah(swt) has ninety-nine names and the one who recites them shall go to heaven(Sahih Bukhari,6410 and Sahih Muslim,2677)\nThis does not mean that Allah(swt) has ninety-nine names only but that anyone who recites ninety-nine names shall go to heaven. Allah(swt) has many more names than these.\nAllah(swt) says in the Holy Quran:\nقُلِ ادْعُوا اللَّـهَ أَوِ ادْعُوا الرَّحْمَـٰنَ ۖ أَيًّا مَّا تَدْعُوا فَلَهُ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ ۚ\nSay, \"Call upon Allah or call upon the Most Merciful. Whichever [name] you call - to Him belong the best names.\"\n[Bani-Israel: 110]\n﴿وَلِلَّـهِ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ فَادْعُوهُ بِهَا ۖ وَذَرُوا الَّذِينَ يُلْحِدُونَ فِي أَسْمَائِهِ ۚ سَيُجْزَوْنَ مَا كَانُوا يَعْمَلُونَ ١٨٠﴾\nAnd to Allah belong the best names, so invoke Him by them. And leave [the company of] those who practice deviation concerning His names. They will be recompensed for what they have been doing.\n[Al-Araf: 180]\nThis means that we should neither address Allah(swt) by any name which can even remotely belie His absolute Superiority nor ascribe any random meaning to His unique names. We should take care not to give similar names to anything else in His creation because ultimately all such things pave the way for ‘shirk’ which is the one major sin we have to avoid to escape the everlasting torment.\nAllah(swt) warns in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِذْ قَالَ لُقْمَانُ لِابْنِهِ وَهُوَ يَعِظُهُ يَا بُنَيَّ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِاللَّـهِ ۖ إِنَّ الشِّرْكَ لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيمٌ ١٣﴾\nAnd [mention, O Muhammad], when Luqman said to his son while he was instructing him, \"O my son, do not associate [anything] with Allah. Indeed, association [with him] is great injustice.\"\n[Lukhman: 13]\nHistory proves that the one main reason for ‘shirk’ among the previous tribes was their blasphemy with respect to the Holy names of Allah(swt) and the distortion of their sublime meanings. For instance the Jews used the name ‘Yehova’ which means the Sustainer of Jews. The Christians call Him ‘Father’ who has a son (inna Aoozubillah). Similarly many other tribes started using such names for Allah(swt) which resembled the things in His creation. Gradually these things became their gods. In the Hindu scriptures the word ‘Savita’ is used for god which is another name for sun. So as time went by sun also became their god.\nIn the same way the idol-worshippers of Makkah derived the name of the idol ‘Uzza’ from His holy name ‘Aziz’ and ‘Laat’ from His holy name ‘Ilaah’ and started worshipping them.\nAllah(swt) declares in the Holy Quran:\n﴿لَيْسَ كَمِثْلِهِ شَيْءٌ ۖ وَهُوَ السَّمِيعُ الْبَصِيرُ ١١﴾\nThere is nothing like unto Him, and He is the Hearing, the Seeing.\n[Ash-shura: 11]\nHe(swt) is not without any attributes but the possessor of the most beautiful and supreme qualities. At the same time He(swt) is unique and different from anything in His creation. That is why we should be extremely cautious with respect to His names. His names should be solely on the basis of the Holy Quran and Sahih Hadith. The various names of Allah which occur in the Islamic scriptures are described in detail in Tirmizi (3507) and Ibn-Maaza(3861). Scholars are of the opinion that these names were never mentioned by the Holy Prophet(saws) but the people themselves collected them. Hence their veracity is doubtful. The Holy Prophet(saws) never mentioned the ninety-nine names but left it to the scholars to derive them in the light of the Holy Quran and Sahih Hadith. Given below is a list of the names which the religious scholars have arrived at:\n\n﻿\nApart from these ninety-nine names, Allah(swt) has many more beautiful names which can be found in the Holy Quran and the Sahih Hadith. According to Sahih Hadith the one who recites these ninety-nine names shall go to heaven. Reciting them means to base all our actions on them and never violate them. For example when we say Allah(swt) is ‘Ilaah’ we should worship Him and Him alone. When we say He(swt) is ‘Ghaffar’ we should seek forgiveness only from Him. When we say He(swt) is ‘Aleem’ we should realize that only He(swt) has the knowledge of the unseen. When we say He(swt) is ‘Mujeeb’ we should seek favours only from Him for He(swt) is the only One who answers our prayers. He(swt) is ‘Raaziq’ so we should seek and expect livelihood from Him alone and no peer, fakir or saint can harm or benefit us in any way.\nAccording to a hadith:\nYou shall get whatever is destined for you; so be righteous in whatever you seek.\nHence, reciting the names of Allah(swt) means to lead our lives according to them."],[42,"§As-Sahabul A’raf\n‘A’raf’ means ‘ a high or elevated place’. ‘As-Sahabul A’raf’ means ‘people of a high place’. Scholars say that between heaven and hell there would be a high wall on which a few people would be seated. This is explained in Surah Hadeed as follows:\n﴿يَوْمَ يَقُولُ الْمُنَافِقُونَ وَالْمُنَافِقَاتُ لِلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا انظُرُونَا نَقْتَبِسْ مِن نُّورِكُمْ قِيلَ ارْجِعُوا وَرَاءَكُمْ فَالْتَمِسُوا نُورًا فَضُرِبَ بَيْنَهُم بِسُورٍ لَّهُ بَابٌ بَاطِنُهُ فِيهِ الرَّحْمَةُ وَظَاهِرُهُ مِن قِبَلِهِ الْعَذَابُ ١٣﴾\nOn the [same] Day the hypocrite men and hypocrite women will say to those who believed, \"Wait for us that we may acquire some of your light.\" It will be said, \"Go back behind you and seek light.\" And a wall will be placed between them with a door, its interior containing mercy, but on the outside of it is torment.\n[Al-Hadeed: 13]\nNow the question arises as to who these ‘As-Sahabul A’raf’ are? Many of the companions(Sahaba) of the Holy Prophet(saws) are of the opinion that these are the people whose good deeds are exactly equal to their bad deeds, so they can neither go to heaven nor enter Hell. The Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَبَيْنَهُمَا حِجَابٌ ۚ وَعَلَى الْأَعْرَافِ رِجَالٌ يَعْرِفُونَ كُلًّا بِسِيمَاهُمْ ۚ وَنَادَوْا أَصْحَابَ الْجَنَّةِ أَن سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ ۚ لَمْ يَدْخُلُوهَا وَهُمْ يَطْمَعُونَ ٤٦﴾\nAnd between them will be a partition, and on [its] elevations are men who recognize all by their mark. And they call out to the companions of Paradise, \"Peace be upon you.\" They have not [yet] entered it, but they long intensely.\n[Al-A’raf: 46]\n﴿وَإِذَا صُرِفَتْ أَبْصَارُهُمْ تِلْقَاءَ أَصْحَابِ النَّارِ قَالُوا رَبَّنَا لَا تَجْعَلْنَا مَعَ الْقَوْمِ الظَّالِمِينَ ٤٧ وَنَادَىٰ أَصْحَابُ الْأَعْرَافِ رِجَالًا يَعْرِفُونَهُم بِسِيمَاهُمْ قَالُوا مَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنكُمْ جَمْعُكُمْ وَمَا كُنتُمْ تَسْتَكْبِرُونَ ٤٨ أَهَـٰؤُلَاءِ الَّذِينَ أَقْسَمْتُمْ لَا يَنَالُهُمُ اللَّـهُ بِرَحْمَةٍ ۚ ادْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْكُمْ وَلَا أَنتُمْ تَحْزَنُونَ ٤٩﴾\nAnd when their eyes are turned toward the companions of the Fire, they say, \"Our Lord, do not place us with the wrongdoing people.\" And the companions of the Elevations will call to men [within Hell] whom they recognize by their mark, saying, \"Of no avail to you was your gathering and [the fact] that you were arrogant.\" [Allah will say], \"Are these the ones whom you [inhabitants of Hell] swore that Allah would never offer them mercy? Enter Paradise, [O People of the Elevations]. No fear will there be concerning you, nor will you grieve.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 47-49]"],[43,"§As-Sahabul Aika\n‘As-Sahabul Aika’ means ‘the people of the jungle’. Prophet Shuaib(as) was sent to the people of Madyan and those living in the jungles. Madyan is the name of the city established near Tabuk on the shores of Qulzum(Clysma), by ‘Midyan’ who was the son of Ibraheem(as) and is thus named after him. His mother was Katura who is known as ‘Madna’ in the Holy Bible. (Refer to : Genesis 25:3). To the south of this city was a forest, the inhabitants of which were called ‘As-Sahabul Aika’. A Greek geologist had written about this forest about a hundred years before the revelation of the Holy Quran. (Sulaiman Nadvi, Arzul-Quran: p.268)\nThis jungle is also described in many interpretations of the Holy Quran. Ibn-Abbas has also written about this forest.\nProphet Isaiah(as) has also described this forest as follows:\nYou caravans of Dedanites, who camp in the thickets of Arabia\n(Bible-Isaiah 21:13)\nProphet Isaiah(as) would warn them about Bukht Nasar. Among those were Arabs also who would also be attacked by Bukht Nasar. This was because he saw that the ‘Aika’ people were transgressing. Instead of worshipping Allah(swt), the One and Only Lord, they had erected various gods and goddesses. So, they were warned of a terrible punishment from Allah(swt).\n‘As-Sahabul Aika’ are mentioned in four places in the Holy Quran:\n﴿وَإِن كَانَ أَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ لَظَالِمِينَ ٧٨ فَانتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْ وَإِنَّهُمَا لَبِإِمَامٍ مُّبِينٍ ٧٩﴾\nAnd the companions of the thicket were [also] wrong-doers. So, We took retribution from them, and indeed, both [cities] are on a clear highway.\n[Al-Hijr: 78-79]\nHere by the two cities are meant, the forest people who were from the tribe of prophet Shuaib(as) and before them the tribe of prophet Lut(as). Both these cities are situated on the path from Mecca to Palestine and Syria. The inhabitants of both these places rejected their prophets and persecuted them so Allah(swt) seized them in a terrible punishment. At one place the Holy Quran explains in more detail about these people of the forest:\n﴿كَذَّبَ أَصْحَابُ الْأَيْكَةِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ١٧٦ إِذْ قَالَ لَهُمْ شُعَيْبٌ أَلَا تَتَّقُونَ ١٧٧ إِنِّي لَكُمْ رَسُولٌ أَمِينٌ ١٧٨ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّـهَ وَأَطِيعُونِ ١٧٩ وَمَا أَسْأَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مِنْ أَجْرٍ ۖ إِنْ أَجْرِيَ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ ١٨٠ أَوْفُوا الْكَيْلَ وَلَا تَكُونُوا مِنَ الْمُخْسِرِينَ ١٨١ وَزِنُوا بِالْقِسْطَاسِ الْمُسْتَقِيمِ ١٨٢ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ أَشْيَاءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِي الْأَرْضِ مُفْسِدِينَ ١٨٣ وَاتَّقُوا الَّذِي خَلَقَكُمْ وَالْجِبِلَّةَ الْأَوَّلِينَ ١٨٤ قَالُوا إِنَّمَا أَنتَ مِنَ الْمُسَحَّرِينَ ١٨٥ وَمَا أَنتَ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا وَإِن نَّظُنُّكَ لَمِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ ١٨٦ فَأَسْقِطْ عَلَيْنَا كِسَفًا مِّنَ السَّمَاءِ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ ١٨٧ قَالَ رَبِّي أَعْلَمُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ ١٨٨ فَكَذَّبُوهُ فَأَخَذَهُمْ عَذَابُ يَوْمِ الظُّلَّةِ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ عَظِيمٍ ١٨٩﴾\nThe companions of the thicket denied the messengers. When Shu'ayb said to them, \"Will you not fear Allah? Indeed, I am to you a trustworthy messenger. So fear Allah and obey me. And I do not ask you for it any payment. My payment is only from the Lord of the worlds. Give full measure and do not be of those who cause loss. And weigh with an even balance. And do not deprive people of their due and do not commit abuse on earth, spreading corruption. And fear He who created you and the former creation.\" They said, \"You are only of those affected by magic. You are but a man like ourselves, and indeed, we think you are among the liars. So cause to fall upon us fragments of the sky, if you should be of the truthful.\" He said, \"My Lord is most knowing of what you do.\" And they denied him, so the punishment of the day of the black cloud seized them. Indeed, it was the punishment of a terrible day.\n[Ash-Shu’ara: 176-189]\nBy ‘the punishment of the day of the black cloud’ is meant that when black clouds appeared, they thought that it was going to rain. But instead of water, it rained fire and all of them were burnt to ashes.\nIn the Surah Sad, the people of the forest are described along with the other disbelievers who rejected the messengers of Allah(swt) and were thus seized by Him in a terrible punishment. Among them are the tribes of Nuh(as), Aad, Thamud, the tribe of Pharaoh, the owner of stakes, the people of the forest(thicket) and the tribe of Lut(as). After describing all these tribes the Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِن كُلٌّ إِلَّا كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ عِقَابِ ١٤﴾\nEach of them denied the messengers, so My penalty was justified.\n[Sad: 14]\nSimilarly in Surah Qaf, the people of the forest have been described along with those tribes who had rejected their prophets; namely the tribe of Nuh(as), the people of Rass, the tribe of Aad and Thamud, the tribe of Pharaoh, the tribe of Lut(as), the people of the forest(thicket) and the people of Tubba.\n﴿كُلٌّ كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيدِ ١٤﴾\nAll denied the messengers, so My threat was justly fulfilled.\n[Qaf: 14]\nThe punishment of Allah(swt) seized these people of the forest. Whatever remained, the conqueror Bukht Nasar of the 6th century B.C. wiped out in his attacks, as was predicted by prophet Isaiah(as)."],[44,"§As-Sahabul Feel\nAs-Sahabul Feel means ‘elephant people’. The Arabic word for elephant is ‘feel’. This is described at one place in the Holy Quran and a surah with the same name was revealed. It consists of a total of five verses whose translation is as follows:\n﴿أَلَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِأَصْحَابِ الْفِيلِ ١ أَلَمْ يَجْعَلْ كَيْدَهُمْ فِي تَضْلِيلٍ ٢ وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ ٣ تَرْمِيهِم بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّن سِجِّيلٍ ٤ فَجَعَلَهُمْ كَعَصْفٍ مَّأْكُولٍ ٥﴾\nHave you not considered, [O Muhammad], how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant? Did He not make their plan into misguidance? And He sent against them birds in flocks, Striking them with stones of hard clay, And He made them like eaten straw.\n[Al-Feel: 1-5]\nThe event of the elephant people took place around 570-571 A.D. and it was the year of the birth of the Holy Prophet(saws). Briefly the story of the elephant people is as follows:\nThere were two leaders in Yemen – Arwat and Abraha. Abraha is the distorted form of Ibraheem. For some reason these two fought among themselves and Arwat was killed. When the African king Nazzashi came to know this he was furious and vowed to destroy Abraha. When Abraha heard this he wrote to the king that he would build such a church in Yemen the like of which would not be found anywhere else in the world and he also sought his forgiveness for the crime. This made the king happy because even he wanted Christianity to be propagated in the Arabian peninsula.Abraha built a big church and ordered the Arabs to perform the pilgrimage to this place instead of the Holy Kaaba in Mecca. But nobody paid heed to his order. So he decided to break down the Holy Kaaba so that people would stop going there and come to his church. So, he assembled a huge army which also consisted of elephants, so that the Arabs would be intimidated.\nWhen Abraha neared Mecca, the people of Quraish realised that they were no match to his huge army. So, they evacuated Mecca and ran away into the mountains. Before going away they prayed near Kaaba saying “O Allah(swt)! Please protect your house as we cannot fight Abraha’s army”.Then they climbed the mountain peaks to watch what would happen to the army.\nReferring to this the Holy Quran says:\n﴿وَأَرْسَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ طَيْرًا أَبَابِيلَ ٣ تَرْمِيهِم بِحِجَارَةٍ مِّن سِجِّيلٍ ٤﴾\nAnd He sent against them birds in flocks, Striking them with stones of hard clay\n[Al-Feel: 3-4]\nIt is said that a huge flock of birds came from the Red Sea. Each bird had one pebble in its beak and two in its claws. Whoever was struck with the pebbles would collapse there itself. Through this surah Allah(swt) is reminding the people of Mecca as to how he had protected them against Abraha and in return, they were disbelieving His Last Prophet(saws). This is also a warning to them that if they persist in their disbelief, a similar retribution from Allah(swt) may befall them. After just a few days, Christianity lost its hold in Yemen. In 575 A.D. Iran captured it and the Irani regime ended when in 628 A.D. the Irani governor embraced Islam. In this way, Christianity was rooted out from Yemen."],[45,"§As-Sahabul Hijr\nAs-Sahabul Hijr means ‘the inhabitants of Hijr’. ‘Hijr’ is the name of a city which was a centre of the tribe of ‘Thamud’. This city has been destroyed, but another city has been found near it which is called ‘Madayan-Saleh’. The well from which the she-camel of prophet Saleh(as) drank water is still in existence there. But the people of Hijr killed it and rejected the call of prophet Saleh(as) and so they were punished by Allah(swt).\n﴿وَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ أَصْحَابُ الْحِجْرِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ ٨٠ وَآتَيْنَاهُمْ آيَاتِنَا فَكَانُوا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِينَ ٨١ وَكَانُوا يَنْحِتُونَ مِنَ الْجِبَالِ بُيُوتًا آمِنِينَ ٨٢ فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ مُصْبِحِينَ ٨٣ فَمَا أَغْنَىٰ عَنْهُم مَّا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ ٨٤﴾\nAnd certainly did the companions of Thamud deny the messengers. And We gave them Our signs, but from them they were turning away. And they used to carve from the mountains, houses, feeling secure. But the shriek seized them at early morning. So nothing availed them [from] what they used to earn.\n[Al-Hijr: 80-84]\nFurther description can be found under ‘Saleh’ and ‘Thamud’."],[46,"§As-Sahabul Jannat\n‘As-Sahabul Jannat’ means ‘the people of the garden’. At one place in the Holy Quran, the people of the garden are described as follows:\n﴿إِنَّا بَلَوْنَاهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَا أَصْحَابَ الْجَنَّةِ إِذْ أَقْسَمُوا لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ ١٧﴾\nIndeed, We have tried them as We tried the companions of the garden, when they swore to cut its fruit in the [early] morning.\n[Al-Qalam: 17]\nWho were these ‘people of the garden’? No further description is given either in the Holy Quran or the Sahih Hadith. But from the way they are described in the Holy Quran, it seems that the people of Mecca were well aware of them. That is why they are being compared to the people of Mecca and are being reminded that Allah(swt) had bestowed many favors upon them. The greatest of the favors is that the last Prophet Muhammad(saws), who was a messenger to the whole of humanity was sent to them. No other messenger will come after him and so it is necessary that they believe in him. But they rejected him. Now, these people of Mecca are being compared to the people of the garden and are being told about what happened to them :\n﴿إِنَّا بَلَوْنَاهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَا أَصْحَابَ الْجَنَّةِ إِذْ أَقْسَمُوا لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ ١٧ وَلَا يَسْتَثْنُونَ ١٨ فَطَافَ عَلَيْهَا طَائِفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمْ نَائِمُونَ ١٩ فَأَصْبَحَتْ كَالصَّرِيمِ ٢٠﴾\nIndeed, We have tried them as We tried the companions of the garden, when they swore to cut its fruit in the [early] morning. Without making exception. So there came upon the garden an affliction from your Lord while they were asleep. And it became as though reaped.\n[Al-Qalam: 17-20]\nThe other lesson which we learn from this is that it is a must for us to say ‘Insha-Allah’ (meaning if Allah(swt) Wills), when we desire to do something. As it says in Surah Al-Kahf:\n﴿وَلَا تَقُولَنَّ لِشَيْءٍ إِنِّي فَاعِلٌ ذَٰلِكَ غَدًا ٢٣ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ اللَّـهُ ۚ وَاذْكُر رَّبَّكَ إِذَا نَسِيتَ وَقُلْ عَسَىٰ أَن يَهْدِيَنِ رَبِّي لِأَقْرَبَ مِنْ هَـٰذَا رَشَدًا ٢٤﴾\nAnd never say of anything, \"Indeed, I will do that tomorrow,\" Except [when adding], \"If Allah wills.\" And remember your Lord when you forget [it] and say, \"Perhaps my Lord will guide me to what is nearer than this to right conduct.\"\n[Al-Kahf: 23-24]\nThat is always say ‘Insha-Allah’. It is said that it was the custom of those days that when the owner of the garden went to cut the fruit, he would distribute some among the poor too. This is also confirmed in the teachings of Isa(as).\nThe owners of the gardens described in the above verses thought that when they themselves made ends meet with great difficulty, why should they share the fruit with the poor. So, they decided to go very early to the gardens and cut the fruit so that the poor did not come to know of it. While they were plotting thus, Allah(swt) was also planning. The above incident is described as follows in the Holy Quran:\n﴿فَأَصْبَحَتْ كَالصَّرِيمِ ٢٠ فَتَنَادَوْا مُصْبِحِينَ ٢١ أَنِ اغْدُوا عَلَىٰ حَرْثِكُمْ إِن كُنتُمْ صَارِمِينَ ٢٢ فَانطَلَقُوا وَهُمْ يَتَخَافَتُونَ ٢٣ أَن لَّا يَدْخُلَنَّهَا الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكُم مِّسْكِينٌ ٢٤ وَغَدَوْا عَلَىٰ حَرْدٍ قَادِرِينَ ٢٥ فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهَا قَالُوا إِنَّا لَضَالُّونَ ٢٦ بَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُومُونَ ٢٧ قَالَ أَوْسَطُهُمْ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكُمْ لَوْلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ ٢٨ قَالُوا سُبْحَانَ رَبِّنَا إِنَّا كُنَّا ظَالِمِينَ ٢٩ فَأَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَلَاوَمُونَ ٣٠ قَالُوا يَا وَيْلَنَا إِنَّا كُنَّا طَاغِينَ ٣١ عَسَىٰ رَبُّنَا أَن يُبْدِلَنَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهَا إِنَّا إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا رَاغِبُونَ ٣٢﴾\nAnd it became as though reaped. And they called one another at morning, [Saying], \"Go early to your crop if you would cut the fruit.\" So they set out, while lowering their voices, [Saying], \"There will surely not enter it today upon you [any] poor person.\" And they went early in determination, [assuming themselves] able. But when they saw it, they said, \"Indeed, we are lost; Rather, we have been deprived.\" The most moderate of them said, \"Did I not say to you, 'Why do you not exalt [Allah]?' \"They said, \"Exalted is our Lord! Indeed, we were wrongdoers.\" Then they approached one another, blaming each other. They said, \"O woe to us; indeed we were transgressors. Perhaps our Lord will substitute for us [one] better than it. Indeed, we are toward our Lord desirous.\"\n[Al-Qalam: 20-32]\nAccording to Ibn-Abbas, this garden was in Yemen, while some other scholars say that it was in Habsha. Wherever it was, through this narration, Allah(swt) is warning the people of Mecca that if they behave in a similar fashion, then they too would suffer the same fate as the people of the garden. Even they would be destroyed because Allah(swt) is All-Powerful. So, it is imperative that in return for the favors bestowed upon them by Allah(swt), they believe in the last Prophet(saws) or else neither their wealth nor their children will avail them.\n﴿كَذَٰلِكَ الْعَذَابُ ۖ وَلَعَذَابُ الْآخِرَةِ أَكْبَرُ ۚ لَوْ كَانُوا يَعْلَمُونَ ٣٣﴾\nSuch is the punishment [of this world]. And the punishment of the Hereafter is greater, if they only knew.\n[Al-Qalam: 33]\nOther than this wherever ‘As-Sahabul Jannat’ are mentioned, what is meant is ‘people of the heaven’ as in Surah Baqra(2:82), Surah Al-A’raf(7:42), Surah Yunus(10:26), Surah Hud(11:23) etc. These are the people who shall enter heaven. The opposite of this is ‘As-Sahab-un-naar’ which means ‘people of the hell’ that is the people who shall go to hell. So, one day the dwellers of heaven will call out to the dwellers of hell :\n﴿وَنَادَىٰ أَصْحَابُ الْجَنَّةِ أَصْحَابَ النَّارِ أَن قَدْ وَجَدْنَا مَا وَعَدَنَا رَبُّنَا حَقًّا فَهَلْ وَجَدتُّم مَّا وَعَدَ رَبُّكُمْ حَقًّا ۖ قَالُوا نَعَمْ ۚ فَأَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ بَيْنَهُمْ أَن لَّعْنَةُ اللَّـهِ عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ ٤٤﴾\nAnd the companions of Paradise will call out to the companions of the Fire, \"We have already found what our Lord promised us to be true. Have you found what your Lord promised to be true?\" They will say, \"Yes.\" Then an announcer will announce among them, \"The curse of Allah shall be upon the wrongdoers.\"\n[Al-A’raf: 44]"],[47,"§As-Sahabul Kahf\n‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ means the people living in caves.\nThese were a group of about nine youth who had taken shelter in a mountain cave when the cruelties of the tyrant ruler became unbearable. Then a miracle occurred about which the Arabs had some knowledge. When they wished to know all the details about this miracle, Surah Kahf was revealed in which Allah(swt) says:\n﴿أَمْ حَسِبْتَ أَنَّ أَصْحَابَ الْكَهْفِ وَالرَّقِيمِ كَانُوا مِنْ آيَاتِنَا عَجَبًا ٩ إِذْ أَوَى الْفِتْيَةُ إِلَى الْكَهْفِ فَقَالُوا رَبَّنَا آتِنَا مِن لَّدُنكَ رَحْمَةً وَهَيِّئْ لَنَا مِنْ أَمْرِنَا رَشَدًا ١٠ فَضَرَبْنَا عَلَىٰ آذَانِهِمْ فِي الْكَهْفِ سِنِينَ عَدَدًا ١١ ثُمَّ بَعَثْنَاهُمْ لِنَعْلَمَ أَيُّ الْحِزْبَيْنِ أَحْصَىٰ لِمَا لَبِثُوا أَمَدًا ١٢ نَّحْنُ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ نَبَأَهُم بِالْحَقِّ ۚ إِنَّهُمْ فِتْيَةٌ آمَنُوا بِرَبِّهِمْ وَزِدْنَاهُمْ هُدًى ١٣ وَرَبَطْنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ إِذْ قَامُوا فَقَالُوا رَبُّنَا رَبُّ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ لَن نَّدْعُوَ مِن دُونِهِ إِلَـٰهًا ۖ لَّقَدْ قُلْنَا إِذًا شَطَطًا ١٤ هَـٰؤُلَاءِ قَوْمُنَا اتَّخَذُوا مِن دُونِهِ آلِهَةً ۖ لَّوْلَا يَأْتُونَ عَلَيْهِم بِسُلْطَانٍ بَيِّنٍ ۖ فَمَنْ أَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرَىٰ عَلَى اللَّـهِ كَذِبًا ١٥ وَإِذِ اعْتَزَلْتُمُوهُمْ وَمَا يَعْبُدُونَ إِلَّا اللَّـهَ فَأْوُوا إِلَى الْكَهْفِ يَنشُرْ لَكُمْ رَبُّكُم مِّن رَّحْمَتِهِ وَيُهَيِّئْ لَكُم مِّنْ أَمْرِكُم مِّرْفَقًا ١٦ وَتَرَى الشَّمْسَ إِذَا طَلَعَت تَّزَاوَرُ عَن كَهْفِهِمْ ذَاتَ الْيَمِينِ وَإِذَا غَرَبَت تَّقْرِضُهُمْ ذَاتَ الشِّمَالِ وَهُمْ فِي فَجْوَةٍ مِّنْهُ ۚ ذَٰلِكَ مِنْ آيَاتِ اللَّـهِ ۗ مَن يَهْدِ اللَّـهُ فَهُوَ الْمُهْتَدِ ۖ وَمَن يُضْلِلْ فَلَن تَجِدَ لَهُ وَلِيًّا مُّرْشِدًا ١٧ وَتَحْسَبُهُمْ أَيْقَاظًا وَهُمْ رُقُودٌ ۚ وَنُقَلِّبُهُمْ ذَاتَ الْيَمِينِ وَذَاتَ الشِّمَالِ ۖ وَكَلْبُهُم بَاسِطٌ ذِرَاعَيْهِ بِالْوَصِيدِ ۚ لَوِ اطَّلَعْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ لَوَلَّيْتَ مِنْهُمْ فِرَارًا وَلَمُلِئْتَ مِنْهُمْ رُعْبًا ١٨ وَكَذَٰلِكَ بَعَثْنَاهُمْ لِيَتَسَاءَلُوا بَيْنَهُمْ ۚ قَالَ قَائِلٌ مِّنْهُمْ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ ۖ قَالُوا لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا أَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ ۚ قَالُوا رَبُّكُمْ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا لَبِثْتُمْ فَابْعَثُوا أَحَدَكُم بِوَرِقِكُمْ هَـٰذِهِ إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ فَلْيَنظُرْ أَيُّهَا أَزْكَىٰ طَعَامًا فَلْيَأْتِكُم بِرِزْقٍ مِّنْهُ وَلْيَتَلَطَّفْ وَلَا يُشْعِرَنَّ بِكُمْ أَحَدًا ١٩ إِنَّهُمْ إِن يَظْهَرُوا عَلَيْكُمْ يَرْجُمُوكُمْ أَوْ يُعِيدُوكُمْ فِي مِلَّتِهِمْ وَلَن تُفْلِحُوا إِذًا أَبَدًا ٢٠ وَكَذَٰلِكَ أَعْثَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَعْلَمُوا أَنَّ وَعْدَ اللَّـهِ حَقٌّ وَأَنَّ السَّاعَةَ لَا رَيْبَ فِيهَا إِذْ يَتَنَازَعُونَ بَيْنَهُمْ أَمْرَهُمْ ۖ فَقَالُوا ابْنُوا عَلَيْهِم بُنْيَانًا ۖ رَّبُّهُمْ أَعْلَمُ بِهِمْ ۚ قَالَ الَّذِينَ غَلَبُوا عَلَىٰ أَمْرِهِمْ لَنَتَّخِذَنَّ عَلَيْهِم مَّسْجِدًا ٢١ سَيَقُولُونَ ثَلَاثَةٌ رَّابِعُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ وَيَقُولُونَ خَمْسَةٌ سَادِسُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ رَجْمًا بِالْغَيْبِ ۖ وَيَقُولُونَ سَبْعَةٌ وَثَامِنُهُمْ كَلْبُهُمْ ۚ قُل رَّبِّي أَعْلَمُ بِعِدَّتِهِم مَّا يَعْلَمُهُمْ إِلَّا قَلِيلٌ ۗ فَلَا تُمَارِ فِيهِمْ إِلَّا مِرَاءً ظَاهِرًا وَلَا تَسْتَفْتِ فِيهِم مِّنْهُمْ أَحَدًا ٢٢ وَلَا تَقُولَنَّ لِشَيْءٍ إِنِّي فَاعِلٌ ذَٰلِكَ غَدًا ٢٣ إِلَّا أَن يَشَاءَ اللَّـهُ ۚ وَاذْكُر رَّبَّكَ إِذَا نَسِيتَ وَقُلْ عَسَىٰ أَن يَهْدِيَنِ رَبِّي لِأَقْرَبَ مِنْ هَـٰذَا رَشَدًا ٢٤ وَلَبِثُوا فِي كَهْفِهِمْ ثَلَاثَ مِائَةٍ سِنِينَ وَازْدَادُوا تِسْعًا ٢٥ قُلِ اللَّـهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا لَبِثُوا ۖ لَهُ غَيْبُ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ ۖ أَبْصِرْ بِهِ وَأَسْمِعْ ۚ مَا لَهُم مِّن دُونِهِ مِن وَلِيٍّ وَلَا يُشْرِكُ فِي حُكْمِهِ أَحَدًا ٢٦ وَاتْلُ مَا أُوحِيَ إِلَيْكَ مِن كِتَابِ رَبِّكَ ۖ لَا مُبَدِّلَ لِكَلِمَاتِهِ وَلَن تَجِدَ مِن دُونِهِ مُلْتَحَدًا ٢٧﴾\nOr have you thought that the companions of the cave and the inscription were, among Our signs, a wonder?[Mention] when the youths retreated to the cave and said, \"Our Lord, grant us from Yourself mercy and prepare for us from our affair right guidance.\" So We cast [a cover of sleep] over their ears within the cave for a number of years. Then We awakened them that We might show which of the two factions was most precise in calculating what [extent] they had remained in time. It is We who relate to you, [O Muhammad], their story in truth. Indeed, they were youths who believed in their Lord, and We increased them in guidance. And We made firm their hearts when they stood up and said, \"Our Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth. Never will we invoke besides Him any deity. We would have certainly spoken, then, an excessive transgression. These, our people, have taken besides Him deities. Why do they not bring for [worship of] them a clear authority? And who is more unjust than one who invents about Allah a lie?\"\nAnd [had you been present], you would see the sun when it rose, inclining away from their cave on the right, and when it set, passing away from them on the left, while they were [laying] within an open space thereof. That was from the signs of Allah. He whom Allah guides is the [rightly] guided, but he whom He leaves astray - never will you find for him a protecting guide. And you would think them awake, while they were asleep. And We turned them to the right and to the left, while their dog stretched his forelegs at the entrance. If you had looked at them, you would have turned from them in flight and been filled by them with terror. And similarly, We awakened them that they might question one another. Said a speaker from among them, \"How long have you remained [here]?\" They said, \"We have remained a day or part of a day.\" They said, \"Your Lord is most knowing of how long you remained. So send one of you with this silver coin of yours to the city and let him look to which is the best of food and bring you provision from it and let him be cautious. And let no one be aware of you. Indeed, if they come to know of you, they will stone you or return you to their religion. And never would you succeed, then - ever.\"\nAnd similarly, We caused them to be found that they [who found them] would know that the promise of Allah is truth and that of the Hour there is no doubt. [That was] when they disputed among themselves about their affair and [then] said, \"Construct over them a structure. Their Lord is most knowing about them.\" Said those who prevailed in the matter, \"We will surely take [for ourselves] over them a masjid.\" They will say there were three, the fourth of them being their dog; and they will say there were five, the sixth of them being their dog - guessing at the unseen; and they will say there were seven, and the eighth of them was their dog. Say, [O Muhammad], \"My Lord is most knowing of their number. None knows them except a few. So do not argue about them except with an obvious argument and do not inquire about them among [the speculators] from anyone.\" And never say of anything, \"Indeed, I will do that tomorrow,\" Except [when adding], \"If Allah wills.\" And remember your Lord when you forget [it] and say, \"Perhaps my Lord will guide me to what is nearer than this to right conduct.\" And they remained in their cave for three hundred years and exceeded by nine. Say, \"Allah is most knowing of how long they remained. He has [knowledge of] the unseen [aspects] of the heavens and the earth. How Seeing is He and how Hearing! They have not besides Him any protector, and He shares not His legislation with anyone.\" And recite, [O Muhammad], what has been revealed to you of the Book of your Lord. There is no changer of His words, and never will you find in other than Him a refuge. [Al-Kahf: 9-27]\nFrom this brief description in the Holy Quran we understand that ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ were a group of youth. They believed in Allah(swt) but went and hid in a cave fearing their enemies and that is where Allah(swt) performed a miracle. It is that they slept in the cave for three hundred and nine years. In this way Allah(swt) protected His believers and destroyed their enemies. Allah(swt) revealed this surah to the Holy Prophet(saws) to convince him that similarly He(swt) would take care of the Prophet(saws) and his followers and destroy their enemies. History proves that Allah(swt)’s word came true. Today Islam has spread to every corner of the world while the enemies of Islam have been destroyed.\nNow let us turn the pages of history and see as to who these ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ were and which is the place where this event occurred.\nWe get to know from the history of the Christians that from the first to the fourth century A.D. the Christians had to face a lot of trials. Either the Jews would trouble them and kill countless Christians or the Christians themselves would fight among themselves. After the ascent of Isa(as) to the heavens, the Christians got divided into two groups. The first group believed that Isa(as) was the son of Allah(swt) (Inna Aoozubillah) and that he was blessed with the divine spirit. The second group believed him to be the prophet and slave of Allah(swt) but did not believe in his divinity. As the first group was always in majority, they would torment the second group in various ways. ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ were connected with the second group because Allah(swt) has used the word ‘Momin’ (believers) for them.\nThe question arises whether the tyrant ruler was from the first group or from among the idol-worshippers. Nothing can be said about this from the Holy Quran. The historical ancient book by ‘James Saroji’ which is written in the ‘suryani’ language throws light on this event. Before the advent of Isa(as), the Hebrew language was no longer used, only the Jewish scholars used it. The rest of the people would use the ‘suryani’ language which was a branch of the Hebrew language and was easier. James Saroji was born a few years after the death of As-Sahabul Kahf, that is in the year 452 A.D. He wrote this book around 474 A.D. in which he describes the story of the ‘people of the cave’ or ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ in great detail. The book says that the name of the tyrant ruler was ‘Decius’ whom the historians have described as orthodox. He ruled Rome from 249 to 251 A.D. He tormented the Christians a great deal. They say that he killed about three lakh people as a result of which a few people took refuge in the cave and sleep overtook them. They woke up when Christianity had spread throughout Rome. The scenario had completely changed. Theodosis II was the ruler who had converted to Christianity. When one of the youth went to the city with the old currency, the people were very surprised.\nThe news spread like wild fire and all the people rushed to the cave to have a look at the youth. When the ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ were informed that they had been asleep for three hundred years, even they were surprised. They conveyed their salutations to the people and went back to sleep. They passed away in the same state.\nYaqut Hamvi writes in his book Moazam Buldan(4:274) that Khalifa Wasiq Billah (227-232 A.H.) sent Muhammad bin Musa Khawarijmee to Rome to trace this cave of ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ (that is to Palestine and Syria because these were a part of Rome in those days).His searches led him to a cave at the entrance of which was built a house and a person was seated there. He took him inside the cave where lay thirteen corpses. The person informed him that seven of these were ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’ while the remaining six were kept there for their piety. Their mouths were open and it seemed as if they were asleep. Nothing is known about what happened after that. Accepting this story presents a few difficulties.\nFirstly it is said that they awoke during the reign of Theodosis II who ruled from 408 to 450 A.D. So, the period for which they were asleep works out to around 196 years while the Holy Quran mentions it as 309.\nBut some scholars of the Holy Quran are of the opinion that the period for which they were asleep is not 309 years but it is the opinion of the Christians who felt that they had been sleeping for 309 years. That is why the Holy Quran has not elaborated on this but it says that the exact knowledge about the time period is with Allah(swt) alone. (Refer to Tafseer Ibn-Jarir Tabri, 8:152)\nSecondly the story says that there were seven youth while the Holy Quran says that the exact number is known to Allah(swt) alone.\nThirdly according to the story this event took place at the place called ‘Ifsas’ while the Holy Quran says that the name of the place was ‘Rakhim’ and there exists a place of that name in Palestine. This place is mentioned as ‘Rekem’ in the Holy Bible; which is situated to the west of Jerusalem (Refer to Yehoshu, 18:27).\nDue to the above mentioned reasons this story cannot be the story of ‘As-Sahabul Kahf’. It is possible that a similar event had taken place. The reason is that during the first three centuries when the Christians were being tormented, many of them escaped to the mountain caves and forests and spent their time in the remembrance of their Lord. Referring to them the Holy Quran says:\nوَجَعَلْنَا فِي قُلُوبِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ رَأْفَةً وَرَحْمَةً وَرَهْبَانِيَّةً ابْتَدَعُوهَا مَا كَتَبْنَاهَا عَلَيْهِمْ إِلَّا ابْتِغَاءَ رِضْوَانِ اللَّـهِ\nAnd We placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy and monasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except [that they did so] seeking the approval of Allah.\n[Al-Hadid: 27]"],[48,"§As-Sahabul Khariya\nAs-Sahabul Khariya means the dwellers of the city. The Holy Quran refers to the ‘dwellers of the city’ as follows:\n﴿وَاضْرِبْ لَهُم مَّثَلًا أَصْحَابَ الْقَرْيَةِ إِذْ جَاءَهَا الْمُرْسَلُونَ ١٣ إِذْ أَرْسَلْنَا إِلَيْهِمُ اثْنَيْنِ فَكَذَّبُوهُمَا فَعَزَّزْنَا بِثَالِثٍ فَقَالُوا إِنَّا إِلَيْكُم مُّرْسَلُونَ ١٤ قَالُوا مَا أَنتُمْ إِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا وَمَا أَنزَلَ الرَّحْمَـٰنُ مِن شَيْءٍ إِنْ أَنتُمْ إِلَّا تَكْذِبُونَ ١٥ قَالُوا رَبُّنَا يَعْلَمُ إِنَّا إِلَيْكُمْ لَمُرْسَلُونَ ١٦ وَمَا عَلَيْنَا إِلَّا الْبَلَاغُ الْمُبِينُ ١٧ قَالُوا إِنَّا تَطَيَّرْنَا بِكُمْ ۖ لَئِن لَّمْ تَنتَهُوا لَنَرْجُمَنَّكُمْ وَلَيَمَسَّنَّكُم مِّنَّا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ١٨ قَالُوا طَائِرُكُم مَّعَكُمْ ۚ أَئِن ذُكِّرْتُم ۚ بَلْ أَنتُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّسْرِفُونَ ١٩ وَجَاءَ مِنْ أَقْصَى الْمَدِينَةِ رَجُلٌ يَسْعَىٰ قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ اتَّبِعُوا الْمُرْسَلِينَ ٢٠ اتَّبِعُوا مَن لَّا يَسْأَلُكُمْ أَجْرًا وَهُم مُّهْتَدُونَ ٢١﴾\nAnd present to them an example: the people of the city, when the messengers came to it - When We sent to them two but they denied them, so We strengthened them with a third, and they said, \"Indeed, we are messengers to you.\" They said, \"You are not but human beings like us, and the Most Merciful has not revealed a thing. You are only telling lies.\" They said, \"Our Lord knows that we are messengers to you, And we are not responsible except for clear notification.\" They said, \"Indeed, we consider you a bad omen. If you do not desist, we will surely stone you, and there will surely touch you, from us, a painful punishment.\" They said, \"Your omen is with yourselves. Is it because you were reminded? Rather, you are a transgressing people.\" And there came from the farthest end of the city a man, running. He said, \"O my people, follow the messengers. Follow those who do not ask of you [any] payment, and they are [rightly] guided.\n[Ya-Sin: 13-21]\nThe people of Mecca seemed to be aware of the ‘people of the city’ referred to in these verses because nobody questioned the Holy Prophet(saws) about them and no other details are given either in the Holy Quran or the Sahih Hadith.\nNow the question arises as to who exactly these people were and what was the name of their city? Below is given a brief description of what the commentators of the Holy Quran have written about it:\n1. The most popular exposition which is by Ibn-Abbas, Kaab Ahbar and Wahab-bin-Munabbah says that the name of the city was ‘Antakia’ which is near the border of Syria and Turkey and mentions the names of the three prophets as Saadiq, Sadood and Shaloom. Ibn-Ishaq says that the chain of this narration lacks continuity and thus cannot be accepted. (Refer to Ibn-Jarir Tabri, 22:156)\n2. Some are of the opinion that these three prophets were sent by Isa(as) to ‘Antakia’ for the propagation of religion and that their names were Shamoon, Yuhanna and Bolis.\nThis version is not true because the Christian religious preachers reached Antakia after the ascent (to the heavens) of Isa(as). And somebody who has not been appointed as a prophet by Allah(swt) cannot be called a prophet. It goes against the Holy Quran. And there is no historical record that any calamity had befallen Antakia.\nThe Holy Quran says:\n﴿إِن كَانَتْ إِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَاحِدَةً فَإِذَا هُمْ خَامِدُونَ ٢٩﴾\nIt was not but one shout, and immediately they were extinguished.\n[Ya-sin: 29]\nThat is everyone was destroyed and none remained.\n3. Some scholars feel that by the ‘three prophets’ are meant Musa(as), Isa(as) and Muhammad(saws). All three were sent to the Arabs but just as they rejected Musa(as) and Isa(as), they disbelieved Muhammad(saws) also. If they persist in their disobedience, they would be annihilated with just one shout. ‘The man who came running from the farthest end of the city saying “O my people, follow the messengers”’ means Abu-Bakr according to them.\nBut this explanation does not gel with any verse of the Holy Quran. So, it is better for us to grasp the core message and teachings of this miraculous book from Allah(swt) rather than go into the questions like:\nWhich was the city? Who were the prophets? etc till we get some conclusive proof. By describing about these dwellers of the city, the Holy Quran is inviting the people of Mecca and all others to Islam and warning them about the terrible retribution if they reject the true faith."]])